his sounds so great! we must go!&quot; if you know what I mean <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I don't think we will be there but I absolutely wish everyone attending a really great time!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11694-hexer","name":"Hexer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11694_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"93"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-21T05:06:48-08:00","id":1020296,"title":"","content":"Sounds fun, but the only person I know in German that would like for sure to go isn't talking to me anymore, and I think he leaved the RPG scene for good...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>#NothingAboutUsWithoutUs<br /> #AutismPride<br /> She/her pronouns","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5826-monteparnas","name":"monteparnas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5826_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6710"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-22T15:13:15-08:00","id":1021031,"title":"","content":"I'll be there, for the record, in a fan capacity.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-23T04:15:59-08:00","id":1021219,"title":"","content":"Sweet! Are you seeing the film? Would love to talk to you about Trinity, am a big fan and have been eagerly awaiting the KS's. Whats your pick of the games from WoD? I am a Werewolf and Mage fan, mostly, but have played literally everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 12-23-2016, 07:18 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-24T13:53:41-08:00","id":1021676,"title":"","content":"I am indeed. (Still have to book flights...)<br /> <br /> i can't promise I'll actually have any answers to <b>Trinity</b> questions but I'm prepared to try. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I started with fantasy gamebooks, got <b>Vampire:The Masquerade</b> from first edition and played and (more often) run a lot since, most recently <b>V20</b> with a lot borrowed from <b>Vampire: The Requiem</b> Second Edition. Next may be <b>Demon: The Descent</b>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T03:57:17-08:00","id":1022685,"title":"","content":"I promise not to ask anything inconvenient <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> And we are going to celebrate WoD, after all. My story with rpgs goes back to red box D&amp;D, aged 7, I was so into gamebooks later on though (as soon as they appeared, Warlock of Firetop, etc). Joe Devers death this year has gutted me (among many other things). As for VtM, I picked it up in Leicester when it came out too, and went back the next week to buy Chicago by Night. I fondly remember that, and I think many people have overlooked its significance, it was really a different kind of city book than had been published before, with heavy emphasis on social relationships for (I think it was) over 70 Kindred. It was so in depth for the time. I spend a lot of time looking at my current collection (5 long shelves) and remembering that first core book purchase. And I remember reading that first core book and wondering what the hell else was out there in the World of Darkness, and what the Antediluvians were up to or who they were, and genuinely not having the slightest idea. That's really a big part of what made the first edition of Werewolf so exciting - a lifting of another veil. When I look back now of course its staggering how much development has gone into it, but I'm struck by the impression that the mysteries are still mine to settle, if I wish to, and I think that is what I am most grateful for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-27T06:04:51-08:00","id":1022706,"title":"","content":"I'm hoping I can get someone to buy me the special VTES card pack. I can only travel to the other Berlins in New England at the moment.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/707-etherial","name":"etherial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar707_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"822"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-28T02:59:17-08:00","id":1023169,"title":"","content":"I can try, as Ill be getting that too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-03T14:39:32-08:00","id":1026168,"title":"","content":"This might be old news, but: <a href=\"http://www.worldofdarkness.berlin/single-post/2016/12/31/Scenario-Competition-Write-Your-Two-Page-Pitch-by-January-6th-2017\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.worldofdarkness.berlin/si...nuary-6th-2017</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T03:29:10-08:00","id":1026435,"title":"","content":"been working on an entry the last 2 days...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T15:46:53-08:00","id":1026729,"title":"","content":"Good luck! I hope the whole thing will lead to great scenarios and eventually that it'll be good to the future of WoD. I didn't try to cook up something, since I saw it the first time on fb yesterday and I'm not that good at writing up modules, especially in English. Oh, well, maybe the next one!<br /> <br /> I think that's something that could be better from WWP, namely that they're very focused on the various big LARP events, which isn't a bad thing on itself, but a lot of information circulates only in those circles and groups and fans outside of those, like me get fewer information and later than ideal. It's a bit like feeling left out, if you don't do LARP, or just don't go to the events, regardless of reasons. This competition is something I'd have been happier to see earlier on the WWP page, their own social media pages, newsletter, etc. Especially with the potential of shaping the future of the setting. I think the competition is a great thing I applaud that they're willing to do something like this and I hope the winning scenarios would be readable online after the event. It just would have been good to know about the whole thing earlier and through more channels.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-04-2017, 06:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-04T19:16:17-08:00","id":1026813,"title":"","content":"I run in more than one LARP circle and I'm just hearing about it for the first time today, so you're definitely not the only one left out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-05T11:52:51-08:00","id":1027190,"title":"","content":"Rectification: it's nothing like I'm feeling left out personally. I just think it would have been better to know about it earlier and through different channels too. The way it is, it's just quite limited how many and which people heard about it, which is not ideal, considering the seeming importance of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Post