ons":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/128-dr-ether","name":"Dr Ether","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar128_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T02:55:43-07:00","id":1091033,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1031512#post1031512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The playtests are announced as part of the event, and that is announced on the site. The sale of VtM5 may be done on pre-order at the con, as far as I have heard, but there is no official announcement for that. Yet...</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey man. I'm from Brazil and didn't have the money to attend, if you participated in the playtest or even bought the book, could you tell me how the new edition is? I was curious about changes in the metaplot","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-11T06:31:57-07:00","id":1091095,"title":"","content":"Yeah, this week seems the longest one of the year... Just waiting for spoilers...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T05:25:53-07:00","id":1091488,"title":"","content":"Liking all the news coming out so far:<br /> <br /> Kenneth Hite is developer<br /> Changeling MET is next<br /> Black Dog label is back(I know many people here will dislike that, but I LOVE it)!!!<br /> Authors keep 50% of revenue<br /> First V5 public playtest is tomorrow","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T06:27:14-07:00","id":1091505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091488#post1091488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liking all the news coming out so far:<br /> <br /> First V5 public playtest is tomorrow</div> </div> </div> </div>If you participate,please tell me how it's like :&gt;. Also,just so you know, i met you in Bloodlines,loved the dialogue,Loved the guns even more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T06:48:31-07:00","id":1091512,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091488#post1091488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Liking all the news coming out so far:<br /> <br /> Kenneth Hite is developer<br /> Changeling MET is next<br /> Black Dog label is back(I know many people here will dislike that, but I LOVE it)!!!</div> </div> </div> </div>More that there wasn't really a need for BD. Ham-handed edginess tends to lose more than it gains. Which leads to my reaction to this...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Authors keep 50% of revenue </div> </div> </div>That can't possibly be a very big return. We're talking trpg books, not a successful novel series. And BD might end up shrinking it as adults only titles clog up shelves.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> First V5 public playtest is tomorrow </div> </div> </div>-24 HOURS REMAIN-","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T07:26:27-07:00","id":1091519,"title":"","content":"Here is the news about the world of darkness and its future from today in bullet points:<br /> <br /> Becketts Jyhad Diary to be the setting and metaplot bible of V5<br /> Format will be one slimmer than normal core rulebook with all the game systems for each line starting with Vampire but to encompass eventually one for all 5 original games<br /> The lines will work together but whether they will be balanced to play together is unclear even to them at this stage. Nevertheless I am sure they will try to do so, for now they focus on what they need to develop.<br /> Demon, Changeling, and all other lines that came later may appear in other media formats before their tabletop games arrive<br /> In fact MET LARP rules for Changeling are now announced<br /> The philosophy with KotE is that is if they find someone from the area who can do it they will. They want to avoid the problem of having people write about a culture when they do not know it themselves. So go for it if you live anywhere in Asia and love these games.<br /> The fact that China is making moves around Africa was talked about as being very interesting from the point of the undead sects in those places now having interactions.<br /> Setting material will be presented seperately in huge books related to specific groups the first two being Camrilla and Anarch setting and source books<br /> The setting material will be the reference material for all creative projects from film to larp and tt - and there will be an online hub for sharing every aspect of the wod in every media. Contributors to this &quot;storytelling vault&quot; will be paid 50% of what their contributions earn.<br /> Vampires first two setting books will be Camarilla and Anarch with Sabbat to come later (see below for the metaplot reasons for this). These will release with the core rulebook for V5<br /> Art will involve much photography<br /> Blood Pool is gone. It was described as a gas meter and thus not very sexy. In its place is an elegant and well thought out system relating how you choose to handle hunger to the likelihood of frenzy. You will have composure as a resource. You can opt to spend this when faced with a situation where you want to resist doing something eg feeding at the sight of blood. If you spend it however you get a red hunger die or more in your pools (for probably all your rolls) which will act to increase your chance of entering frenzy. If you dont, you do something you dont want to, avoiding compulsion, but you will have more composure when the chance you frenzy comes up, and less hunger, meaning less likely to frenzy.<br /> Similar mechanics will replace Rage and other power supply traits in the core books for those games.<br /> Over 40 books currently in development. Hopes for an adult tv show by 2020.<br /> System will use dots and d10s and be recognisable to older fans. However some dice may be customised and the inclusion of hunger dice is a sign that further innovations of the d10 system are planned.<br /> Kenneth Hite of Trail of Cthulhu is on the team as V5 developer<br /> Vampires will have two looks, one for the mortal world and one for Elysium<br /> The Masquerade more important than ever<br /> Its so important the Anarchs have had to agree to join the Cam or be exterminated for not following the 1st Tradition<br /> The 2nd Inquisition is underway after government agencies have discovered the truth. And its brutal and ugly.<br /> The 2nd Inquisition ties in with the Technocracy AND Pentex but the vampires have yet to cotton on to how those spies keep outwitting their attempts to stay hidden...seems as if a new and truly ugly Massassa War may be brewing.<br /> The 2nd Impergium is underway with the Garou finally having presumably listened to the Red Talons (and presumably grudgingly accepted the Ratkins purpose) that humanity must be stopped. Werewolves have realised that Gaia is almost dead.<br /> The current world tensions between Islam and the west are in truth just the mortal facet of the Gehenna Wars<br /> The Gehenna Wars have mysteriously called many elders to the east, in something called The Beckoning, the Sabbat have been especially responsive. Some elders are resisting the Beckoning.<br /> Sabbat reveling in the chaos and war of our times and is now seeking out the ancients to utterly destroy them. This may be what The Beckoning relates to. The Sabbat situation is unclear.<br /> Camarilla more secretive than ever and Masquerade strongly enforced.<br /> V5 playtest tomorrow with Mark Rein Hagen in the house to give a keynote address (taking all 5 of my 1st eds to be signed!)<br /> V5 beta test to be released soon after convention so everyone can try it<br /> Documentary on netflix next year (it was good, but I was genuinely upset that OP were not mentioned but V20 obviously was. They did address this in Q&amp;A, talking about an intended audience that is focused on drawing in totally new players and not having enough time to go into everything, but OP is an important part of the story, I mean 8 years without books and then they changed it in style)<br /> My white puppy rocked the house.<br /> <br /> Thats about all I can recall. If you have any burning questions, drop them here and ill try and get a response on the last day tomorrow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-12-2017, 10:58 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T07:48:13-07:00","id":1091531,"title":"","content":"...I am excited, scared, worried and happy at the same time. And half of those things I'm not sure why. Help.<br /> <br /> On a serious note -<br /> I *like* that the metaplot is being pushed forward like this. It sounds exciting, intriguing, and..just fresh.<br /> I am *worried* about the changes of mechanics - no more Rage pools, Blood pools, (presumably Quintessence pools? etc.) and something akin to the new C20 Nightmare Dice for other systems - could be great. Could be..irksome. We'll see, but I think it's important to keep an open mind.<br /> I am *scared* by the fact that they went with a full on second Impergium - The Garou are after the humans now. This will change the tone and nature of Werewolf in general, a LOT. It will be really really tough to pull off right - but on the other hand, I can see how the 'Shifters might be releasing the handbrakes out of pure desparation at this point.<br /> Along with that I am narrowing my eyes at a full second inquisition happening with Government Agency funding - especially with Technocracy and Pentex involvement. Both the Inquisition and the Impergium are drastically increasing the base tensions between the gamelines - which already were high previously, regarding some points. There are a lot of online games out there that manage an uneasy peace between some groups - both those things will make that harder.<br /> <br /> And I am excited that they seem to have a lot of books in planning. How it all will turn out, time will tell.<br /> <br /> The one thing that made me facepalm is their plans of making the current conflicts between the West and Near East a part of the Gehenna Wars. Come on. That wasn't necessary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-12-2017, 10:52 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T07:49:47-07:00","id":1091532,"title":"","content":"My interest in V^2 continues to wane with every revelation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T08:03:05-07:00","id":1091538,"title":"","content":"the ticker tape is coming back and will have current events framed in WoD terms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T08:07:31-07:00","id":1091541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091531#post1091531\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The one thing that made me facepalm is their plans of making the current conflicts between the West and Near East a part of the Gehenna Wars. Come on. That wasn't necessary.</div> </div> </div> </div>They didnt explicitly state that. Thats my inference from what they said and some of the graphics I saw. The actual statement was trhe current state of constant war and trouble in our world is a consequence of the Gehenna Wars.<br /> Overall, the setting is intensifying in line with the intensification of world events<br /> The metaplot weill not be dictation. We are all going to have a major effect on all the metaplot elements. Its going to be something we make happen. Sects will fall based on the choices players of games make. The power they want us to have is that big.<br /> Dice tests will be reduced to a single roll where possible.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-12-2017, 11:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T08:13:47-07:00","id":1091544,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091519#post1091519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the news about the world of darkness and its future from today in bullet points:<br /> <br /> Becketts Jyhad Diary to be the setting and metaplot bible of V5<br /> Format will be one slimmer than normal core rulebook with all the game systems for each line starting with Vampire but to encompass eventually one for all 5 original games<br /> The lines will work together but whether they will be balanced to play together is unclear even to them at this stage. Nevertheless I am sure they will try to do so, for now they focus on what they need to develop.<br /> Demon, Changeling, and all other lines that came later may appear in other media formats before their tabletop games arrive<br /> In fact MET LARP rules for Changeling are now announced<br /> The philosophy with KotE is that is if they find someone from the area who can do it they will. They want to avoid the problem of having people write about a culture when they do not know it themselves. So go for it if you live anywhere in Asia and love these games.<br /> The fact that China is making moves around Africa was talked about as being very interesting from the point of the undead sects in those places now having interactions.<br /> Setting material will be presented seperately in huge books related to specific groups the first two being Camrilla and Anarch setting and source books<br /> The setting material will be the reference material for all creative projects from film to larp and tt - and there will be an online hub for sharing every aspect of the wod in every media. Contributors to this &quot;storytelling vault&quot; will be paid 50% of what their contributions earn.<br /> Vampires first two setting books will be Camarilla and Anarch with Sabbat to come later (see below for the metaplot reasons for this). These will release with the core rulebook for V5<br /> Art will involve much photography<br /> Blood Pool is gone. It was described as a gas meter and thus not very sexy. In its place is an elegant and well thought out system relating how you choose to handle hunger to the likelihood of frenzy. You will have composure as a resource. You can opt to spend this when faced with a situation where you want to resist doing something eg feeding at the sight of blood. If you spend it however you get a red hunger die or more in your pools (for probably all your rolls) which will act to increase your chance of entering frenzy. If you dont, you do something you dont want to, avoiding compulsion, but you will have more composure when the chance you frenzy comes up, and less hunger, meaning less likely to frenzy.<br /> Similar mechanics will replace Rage and other power supply traits in the core books for those games.<br /> Over 40 books currently in development. Hopes for an adult tv show by 2020.<br /> System will use dots and d10s and be recognisable to older fans. However some dice may be customised and the inclusion of hunger dice is a sign that further innovations of the d10 system are planned.<br /> Kenneth Hite of Trail of Cthulhu is on the team as V5 developer<br /> Vampires will have two looks, one for the mortal world and one for Elysium<br /> The Masquerade more important than ever<br /> Its so important the Anarchs have had to agree to join the Cam or be exterminated for not following the 1st Tradition<br /> The 2nd Inquisition is underway after government agencies have discovered the truth. And its brutal and ugly.<br /> The 2nd Inquisition ties in with the Technocracy AND Pentex but the vampires have yet to cotton on to how those spies keep outwitting their attempts to stay hidden...seems as if a new and truly ugly Massassa War may be brewing.<br /> The 2nd Impergium is underway with the Garou finally having presumably listened to the Red Talons (and presumably grudgingly accepted the Ratkins purpose) that humanity must be stopped. Werewolves have realised that Gaia is almost dead.<br /> The current world tensions between Islam and the west are in truth just the mortal facet of the Gehenna Wars<br /> The Gehenna Wars have mysteriously called many elders to the east, in something called The Beckoning, the Sabbat have been especially responsive. Some elders are resisting the Beckoning.<br /> Sabbat reveling in the chaos and war of our times and is now seeking out the ancients to utterly destroy them. This may be what The Beckoning relates to. The Sabbat situation is unclear.<br /> Camarilla more secretive than ever and Masquerade strongly enforced.<br /> V5 playtest tomorrow with Mark Rein Hagen in the house to give a keynote address (taking all 5 of my 1st eds to be signed!)<br /> V5 beta test to be released soon after convention so everyone can try it<br /> Documentary on netflix next year (it was good, but I was genuinely upset that OP were not mentioned but V20 obviously was. They did address this in Q&amp;A, talking about an intended audience that is focused on drawing in totally new players and not having enough time to go into everything, but OP is an important part of the story, I mean 8 years without books and then they changed it in style)<br /> My white puppy rocked the house.<br /> <br /> Thats about all I can recall. If you have any burning questions, drop them here and ill try and get a response on the last day tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi! first things first,thank you for those bullet points. Did gehenna the event happen? And how was the world of darkness changed by it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T08:17:40-07:00","id":1091545,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091541#post1091541\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They didnt explicitly state that. Thats my inference from what they said and some of the graphics I saw. The actual statement was trhe current state of constant war and trouble in our world is a consequence of the Gehenna Wars.<br /> Overall, the setting is intensifying in line with the intensification of world events<br /> The metaplot weill not be dictation. We are all going to have a major effect on all the metaplot elements. Its going to be something we make happen. Sects will fall based on the choices players of games make. The power they want us to have is that big.<br /> Dice tests will be reduced to a single roll where possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh boy. I guarantee my games won't have an effect, because I'm not part of any organized play group.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T08:38:04-07:00","id":1091558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091544#post1091544\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi! first things first,thank you for those bullet points. Did gehenna the event happen? And how was the world of darkness changed by it?</div> </div> </div> </div>That was not revealed. Its a question I will ask at the playtest tomorrow.<br /> Cities are now more like dark ages fiefdoms, with Princes shrinking from communication due to threats and so cities are now more directly characterised by their Prince.<br /> All previous editions will be supported and content for them labelled. For example, if you write a story for 1st edition Vampire, it will be labelled as such. <br /> There will be a new vtm icon. <br /> Italian editions of V5, C20 and VDA20 are coming","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-12-2017, 11:44 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T08:47:45-07:00","id":1091562,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>loomer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091545#post1091545\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh boy. I guarantee my games won't have an effect, because I'm not part of any organized play group.</div> </div> </div> </div>Dont forget this will be multimedia. Computer games for Werewolf (and Vampire got a nod and wink there too) and other interactive media will also play a role here, not just LARPs and tabletop games. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T08:54:25-07:00","id":1091564,"title":"","content":"I'll believe it when I see it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:01:30-07:00","id":1091567,"title":"","content":"First, thank you, deejay for the report! Seriously, I wasn't this excited, anxious and wind-up since waiting for the results of my graduation exam. Every bit of information is just water in the dessert.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091519#post1091519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the news about the world of darkness and its future from today in bullet points:<br /> <br /> Becketts Jyhad Diary to be the setting and metaplot bible of V5<br /> Format will be one slimmer than normal core rulebook with all the game systems for each line starting with Vampire but to encompass eventually one for all 5 original games<br /> The lines will work together but whether they will be balanced to play together is unclear even to them at this stage. Nevertheless I am sure they will try to do so, for now they focus on what they need to develop.<br /> Demon, Changeling, and all other lines that came later may appear in other media formats before their tabletop games arrive<br /> In fact MET LARP rules for Changeling are now announced<br /> The philosophy with KotE is that is if they find someone from the area who can do it they will. They want to avoid the problem of having people write about a culture when they do not know it themselves. So go for it if you live anywhere in Asia and love these games.<br /> The fact that China is making moves around Africa was talked about as being very interesting from the point of the undead sects in those places now having interactions.<br /> Setting material will be presented seperately in huge books related to specific groups the first two being Camrilla and Anarch setting and source books<br /> The setting material will be the reference material for all creative projects from film to larp and tt - and there will be an online hub for sharing every aspect of the wod in every media. Contributors to this &quot;storytelling vault&quot; will be paid 50% of what their contributions earn.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, nothing bad here.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires first two setting books will be Camarilla and Anarch with Sabbat to come later (see below for the metaplot reasons for this). These will release with the core rulebook for V5 </div> </div> </div>It's good they'll have setting books from the get-go.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Art will involve much photography </div> </div> </div>Somewhat sad. I liked the artworks very much on the convention's site, I hoped it will be that direction. I wasn't a fan of photographic artworks in OPP's books, nor in BNS's books. I get the LARP angle of it, but it's just not my preferred style of illustrations, although, it <i>could</i> be good. I just want the new edition to be on par with the older editions so bad...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Blood Pool is gone. It was described as a gas meter and thus not very sexy. In its place is an elegant and well thought out system relating how you choose to handle hunger to the likelihood of frenzy. You will have composure as a resource. You can opt to spend this when faced with a situation where you want to resist doing something eg feeding at the sight of blood. If you spend it however you get a red hunger die or more in your pools (for probably all your rolls) which will act to increase your chance of entering frenzy. If you dont, you do something you dont want to, avoiding compulsion, but you will have more composure when the chance you frenzy comes up, and less hunger, meaning less likely to frenzy.<br /> Similar mechanics will replace Rage and other power supply traits in the core books for those games. </div> </div> </div>Ok, I deliberately won't go into grognardness. It could be good. I don't know how the powers will work without resource-management, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Over 40 books currently in development. Hopes for an adult tv show by 2020. </div> </div> </div>Wait, what????? 40? I'm not sure how I feel about it, I just hope they won't overstretch, or burn through material too fast.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> System will use dots and d10s and be recognisable to older fans. </div> </div> </div>And a great boulder lifted from my heart. At least it won't be rock-paper-scissors, that's already a big plus.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However some dice may be customised and the inclusion of hunger dice is a sign that further innovations of the d10 system are planned. </div> </div> </div>I have some gripes wit the game needing special dice, from a costumer standpoint and it might be a problem with new players, but if executed well and normal d10s could be used for the special dices, I'm not against it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Kenneth Hite of Trail of Cthulhu is on the team as V5 developer </div> </div> </div>He has games in his resume which are up to my alley and games which aren't. He worked on Mage Sorcerers crusade. I hope it'll turn out well. I also hope some of the senior VtM developers, like Eddy Webb will be also in the team. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Vampires will have two looks, one for the mortal world and one for Elysium </div> </div> </div>Wait, like changelings? That's... interesting. It could work, but it's strange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Masquerade more important than ever<br /> Its so important the Anarchs have had to agree to join the Cam or be exterminated for not following the 1st Tradition </div> </div> </div>Hmm. Anarch already were the part of the Cam, in Cam cities. Does this mean that the Cam taken over the Anarch territories and put princes on the seat? If so, why Anarchs need a whole setting book for themselves? I'm not against the latter, my favorite group is the Anarchs, but it seems strange.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The 2nd Inquisition is underway after government agencies have discovered the truth. And its brutal and ugly.<br /> The 2nd Inquisition ties in with the Technocracy AND Pentex but the vampires have yet to cotton on to how those spies keep outwitting their attempts to stay hidden...seems as if a new and truly ugly Massassa War may be brewing.<br /> The 2nd Impergium is underway with the Garou finally having presumably listened to the Red Talons (and presumably grudgingly accepted the Ratkins purpose) that humanity must be stopped. Werewolves have realised that Gaia is almost dead.<br /> The current world tensions between Islam and the west are in truth just the mortal facet of the Gehenna Wars<br /> The Gehenna Wars have mysteriously called many elders to the east, in something called The Beckoning, the Sabbat have been especially responsive. Some elders are resisting the Beckoning.<br /> Sabbat reveling in the chaos and war of our times and is now seeking out the ancients to utterly destroy them. This may be what The Beckoning relates to. The Sabbat situation is unclear.<br /> Camarilla more secretive than ever and Masquerade strongly enforced. </div> </div> </div>All this depends on the execution. I decided I want it to move forward, rather than frozen in time, so okay, big changes coming. I just hope with all my heart it won't be bad writing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 playtest tomorrow with Mark Rein Hagen in the house to give a keynote address (taking all 5 of my 1st eds to be signed!) </div> </div> </div>Tapping, tapping, glancing at the watch, tapping...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> V5 beta test to be released soon after convention so everyone can try it </div> </div> </div>That is a very good decision, big plus in my book! I'm really-really happy if they're taking the public playtest/open dev route!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Documentary on netflix next year (it was good, but I was genuinely upset that OP were not mentioned but V20 obviously was. They did address this in Q&amp;A, talking about an intended audience that is focused on drawing in totally new players and not having enough time to go into everything, but OP is an important part of the story, I mean 8 years without books and then they changed it in style) </div> </div> </div>Hope it'll be a good film to show my non-rpg friends and potential new players. Nothing much to add.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They didnt explicitly state that. Thats my inference from what they said and some of the graphics I saw. The actual statement was trhe current state of constant war and trouble in our world is a consequence of the Gehenna Wars. </div> </div> </div>I'm not against connecting contemporary events and metaplot. Again, good writing is the highest importance. I'm a little wary about supernatural events causing all the fuss, I generally prefer a more balanced approach, but we'll see.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Overall, the setting is intensifying in line with the intensification of world events </div> </div> </div>Seconding a previous poster, I'm not sure how the probability of an all-out war will help crossovers.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The metaplot weill not be dictation. We are all going to have a major effect on all the metaplot elements. Its going to be something we make happen. Sects will fall based on the choices players of games make. The power they want us to have is that big. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. I have doubts, I don't know how well it worked in CCGs, I never participated in those. As long as it doesn't cause the total re-writing of the setting and altering of themes, I'm not necessarily against it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dice tests will be reduced to a single roll where possible. </div> </div> </div>That's why I'm biased about the lead developer... I preferred WoD's system over Trail of Cthulhu, I'm just not big into those kind of games. Also, what about combat? does it mean a serious simplification? I hope not, some streamlining would be good, but please don't overdo it! Also, what about extended tasks, or resisted tasks? How much hours are still until tomorrow, again?????<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:30:19-07:00","id":1091577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091512#post1091512\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> More that there wasn't really a need for BD. Ham-handed edginess tends to lose more than it gains. Which leads to my reaction to this...</div> </div> </div> </div>Most of my favorite WoD books were under that label.<br /> <br /> I don't see much from OP that gives me the same feeling that Charnel Houses of Europe or Freak Legion gave me(and still give me). The quality is mostly there, sure. But there's things missing that's hard to explain. Guess I'm a sucker for 90's stuff. : P<br /> <br /> I would kill for a new Freak Legion, despite loving Book of the Wyrm 20, I felt there were a number of improvements they could've made with numerous chapters.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I know Black Dog is not very popular on these forums, which is fine. I love it, and I'm glad to see it back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> And I'm glad to see Pentex will still be around in 5th Edition. That makes me happy : )","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 05-12-2017, 12:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:37:40-07:00","id":1091581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091577#post1091577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Most of my favorite WoD books were under that label.<br /> <br /> I don't really see much from OP that gives me the same feeling that Charnel Houses of Europe or Freak Legion gave me(and still give me). The quality is mostly there, sure. But there's things missing that's hard to explain.<br /> <br /> I would kill for a new Freak Legion, despite loving Book of the Wyrm 20, I felt there were a number of improvements they could've made with numerous chapters.<br /> <br /> Like I said, I know Black Dog is not very popular on these forums, which is fine. I love it, and I'm glad to see it back. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>I won't fuss about it. One person's &quot;ham-handed edginess&quot; is the other one's &quot;mature content&quot;. I somewhat like edgy, despite how it is a derision nowadays. I also like uncomfortable content. I think it is for the good that they'll have BD again. It'll have some horrible content, that's for sure, but it'll have serious and brilliant ones too, that's the thing with that kind of stuff. I think having the good makes the bad acceptable. I don't have to read books I don't like, but I can't read books which weren't made.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T09:52:19-07:00","id":1091590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091581#post1091581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I won't fuss about it. One person's &quot;ham-handed edginess&quot; is the other one's &quot;mature content&quot;. I somewhat like edgy, despite how it is a derision nowadays. I also like uncomfortable content. I think it is for the good that they'll have BD again. It'll have some horrible content, that's for sure, but it'll have serious and brilliant ones too, that's the thing with that kind of stuff. I think having the good makes the bad acceptable.<b> I don't have to read books I don't like, but I can't read books which weren't made.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed on ALL that you said, but especially the last part.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:19:23-07:00","id":1091606,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091590#post1091590\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Agreed on ALL that you said, but especially the last part.</div> </div> </div> </div>Incidentally, that's the main reason why I got disinterested in WotC current business moedl and in D&amp;D 5e in general, but that's another story.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:32:34-07:00","id":1091612,"title":"","content":"So they're still intent on going full steam ahead with that &quot;2nd Impergium&quot; thing for W:tA? You know, in order to make that a thing that could practically happen, you'd have to massively increase the numbers of Red Talons and extremist fringe camps in other tribes, almost completely kill off the Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, and Glass Walkers (the three most populous tribes of werewolves in the world), massively increase Garou and possibly Fera numbers all around, and also increase their power level to the point where crossover threads wouldn't make any sense because the Garou and/or Fera would be able to completely shut anyone down, isolate them, and then tear them apart.<br /> <br /> All of the prior material has repeated numerous times that a new Impergium can't be done. A few of the reasons appear above, but seriously, the game was made to illustrate that such workings were in the past, to such a degree that human history hadn't started yet. If you want a 2nd Impergium that badly, it'd have to occur in the Renaissance, at the absolute latest, and hence would be an alternate campaign setting. It's not a viable direction going forward with the metaplot, unless you're getting extremely loose with what you mean by &quot;Impergium&quot;.<br /> <br /> And the kicker? It wouldn't even be in the most populous region of the planet. That's primarily Beast Courts territory, and they have a mandate against practicing that sort of thing if you're not helping a wererat, or actually a wererat, and being extremely surreptitious about it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:46:43-07:00","id":1091616,"title":"","content":"Eh. That something is a stupid and impracticable idea never stopped extremists to take an attempt on it anyway.<br /> <br /> My biggest problem with it is that I fear it'll make the setting of Werewolf to a completely desperate one and Werewolves en mass into a very unlikeable group to me and yes it'll mean an end to more open-minded groups. Because of that, I get it as they'll go instead with something very similar to the BNS book, or straight up taking that plot. I don't mind that kind of conflict, I just think it wasn't the most well executed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T10:50:39-07:00","id":1091619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091616#post1091616\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Eh. That something is a stupid and impracticable idea never stopped extremists to take an attempt on it anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>Those groups are in such stark minority that they're hardly ever noticed in the larger body of werewolves. Recall, the three largest tribes in the world are utterly and completely against it. The rest of the tribes are also not for it - even the Red Talons don't think that they could do it. If the most extreme of extremists aren't into it, it's not happening.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> My biggest problem with it is that I fear it'll make the setting of Werewolf to a completely desperate one and Werewolves en mass into a very unlikeable group to me and yes it'll mean an end to more open-minded groups. Because of that, I get it as they'll go instead with something very similar to the BNS book, or straight up taking that plot. I don't mind that kind of conflict, I just think it wasn't the most well executed. </div> </div> </div>No, given all the changes that would have to happen, it would seem to be far less desperate and far more about breaking down doors and mowing down the room without thought or concern. Which the game was moving away from. This entire change is a sharp enough turn and speed to liquefy you from the G-forces.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T11:54:43-07:00","id":1091644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091619#post1091619\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Those groups are in such stark minority that they're hardly ever noticed in the larger body of werewolves. Recall, the three largest tribes in the world are utterly and completely against it. The rest of the tribes are also not for it - even the Red Talons don't think that they could do it. If the most extreme of extremists aren't into it, it's not happening.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, that's the reasonable approach. What if they truly realize that Gaia is dying? That what they're doing for a while just not working at all? Desperate times surged extremism through all of history.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> No, given all the changes that would have to happen, it would seem to be far less desperate and far more about breaking down doors and mowing down the room without thought or concern. Which the game was moving away from. This entire change is a sharp enough turn and speed to liquefy you from the G-forces. </div> </div> </div>Dunno, in my eyes, more reckless violence doesn't mean less desperation, it depends on the backstory.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T12:04:50-07:00","id":1091648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091644#post1091644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, that's the reasonable approach. What if they truly realize that Gaia is dying? That what they're doing for a while just not working at all? Desperate times surged extremism through all of history.</div> </div> </div> </div>A trend I've noticed is that, an awful lot of the time, something that was well-known in Revised is getting repeated in recent material as if it were new. Everyone among the Garou already knew that Gaia is in danger. That's why they started trying to find more effective ways of combating corruption than throwing temper tantrums and swinging at empty air.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Dunno, in my eyes, more reckless violence doesn't mean less desperation, it depends on the backstory. </div> </div> </div>No, I mean, going back to the earlier point, if they can impose something like the Impergium of old, then they have to be at a power level and quantity of werewolves that could somehow utterly destroy anything that would get in their way and generally avoid reprisal attacks and the like. Else, it's not really in Impergium.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T12:13:14-07:00","id":1091652,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091648#post1091648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I mean, going back to the earlier point, if they can impose something like the Impergium of old, then they have to be at a power level and quantity of werewolves that could somehow utterly destroy anything that would get in their way and generally avoid reprisal attacks and the like. Else, it's not really in Impergium.</div> </div> </div> </div>Theoretically, they could just be smart about it. You aren't going to be able to rip out the throats of every human on the planet individually, but modern man is very reliant on infrastructure and this infrastructure is, to Garou thinking, most of the problem anyway. Now, granted, modern law enforcement is good at tracking terrorists, but a lot of that is because they are tracking human terrorists. Folks who talk to other humans, use email and phones, fly on planes, etc. Garou live off the grid, can move and communicate through untraceable and undetectable magic, and keep very much to themselves. Also, their agenda is something law enforcement can't conceive of. Terrorists do a lot of shitty things, but none of them are trying to cause the extinction of the entire human race. So, your eco-terrorist Garou can conceivably do a lot of damage and, with the end of the world at hand, they have literally nothing to lose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T12:24:21-07:00","id":1091658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091652#post1091652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Theoretically, they could just be smart about it. You aren't going to be able to rip out the throats of every human on the planet individually, but modern man is very reliant on infrastructure and this infrastructure is, to Garou thinking, most of the problem anyway. Now, granted, modern law enforcement is good at tracking terrorists, but a lot of that is because they are tracking human terrorists. Folks who talk to other humans, use email and phones, fly on planes, etc. Garou live off the grid, can move and communicate through untraceable and undetectable magic, and keep very much to themselves. Also, their agenda is something law enforcement can't conceive of. Terrorists do a lot of shitty things, but none of them are trying to cause the extinction of the entire human race. So, your eco-terrorist Garou can conceivably do a lot of damage and, with the end of the world at hand, they have literally nothing to lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou aren't trying to make humans extinct, either, except for one tribe, which has less than 500 or so members worldwide. Their ties in this regard are a part of their dilemma. Also, they do have to deal with bans handed down from totems, which might not make this approach as viable as it might be otherwise. Especially if they're totems from the three tribes with the highest number of members, who tend to live with infrastructure or have some aim that might be greatly disrupted from it. It's not like /tg/'s United Druid Front from D&amp;D, which has the advantage of being among the most powerful player character types participating in perfect concert to screw over everyone to whom they have no ties, as well as not having to deal with modern infrastructure and technology on its massive scale (though a number of the modern world's advantages can also be nullified with the capacity to control the weather).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T12:52:49-07:00","id":1091673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091519#post1091519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here is the news about the world of darkness and its future from today in bullet points:<br /> <br /> Becketts Jyhad Diary to be the setting and metaplot bible of V5<br /> Format will be one slimmer than normal core rulebook with all the game systems for each line starting with Vampire but to encompass eventually one for all 5 original games<br /> The lines will work together but whether they will be balanced to play together is unclear even to them at this stage. Nevertheless I am sure they will try to do so, for now they focus on what they need to develop.<br /> Demon, Changeling, and all other lines that came later may appear in other media formats before their tabletop games arrive<br /> In fact MET LARP rules for Changeling are now announced<br /> The philosophy with KotE is that is if they find someone from the area who can do it they will. They want to avoid the problem of having people write about a culture when they do not know it themselves. So go for it if you live anywhere in Asia and love these games.<br /> The fact that China is making moves around Africa was talked about as being very interesting from the point of the undead sects in those places now having interactions.<br /> Setting material will be presented seperately in huge books related to specific groups the first two being Camrilla and Anarch setting and source books<br /> The setting material will be the reference material for all creative projects from film to larp and tt - and there will be an online hub for sharing every aspect of the wod in every media. Contributors to this &quot;storytelling vault&quot; will be paid 50% of what their contributions earn.<br /> Vampires first two setting books will be Camarilla and Anarch with Sabbat to come later (see below for the metaplot reasons for this). These will release with the core rulebook for V5<br /> Art will involve much photography<br /> Blood Pool is gone. It was described as a gas meter and thus not very sexy. In its place is an elegant and well thought out system relating how you choose to handle hunger to the likelihood of frenzy. You will have composure as a resource. You can opt to spend this when faced with a situation where you want to resist doing something eg feeding at the sight of blood. If you spend it however you get a red hunger die or more in your pools (for probably all your rolls) which will act to increase your chance of entering frenzy. If you dont, you do something you dont want to, avoiding compulsion, but you will have more composure when the chance you frenzy comes up, and less hunger, meaning less likely to frenzy.<br /> Similar mechanics will replace Rage and other power supply traits in the core books for those games.<br /> Over 40 books currently in development. Hopes for an adult tv show by 2020.<br /> System will use dots and d10s and be recognisable to older fans. However some dice may be customised and the inclusion of hunger dice is a sign that further innovations of the d10 system are planned.<br /> Kenneth Hite of Trail of Cthulhu is on the team as V5 developer<br /> Vampires will have two looks, one for the mortal world and one for Elysium<br /> The Masquerade more important than ever<br /> Its so important the Anarchs have had to agree to join the Cam or be exterminated for not following the 1st Tradition<br /> The 2nd Inquisition is underway after government agencies have discovered the truth. And its brutal and ugly.<br /> The 2nd Inquisition ties in with the Technocracy AND Pentex but the vampires have yet to cotton on to how those spies keep outwitting their attempts to stay hidden...seems as if a new and truly ugly Massassa War may be brewing.<br /> The 2nd Impergium is underway with the Garou finally having presumably listened to the Red Talons (and presumably grudgingly accepted the Ratkins purpose) that humanity must be stopped. Werewolves have realised that Gaia is almost dead.<br /> The current world tensions between Islam and the west are in truth just the mortal facet of the Gehenna Wars<br /> The Gehenna Wars have mysteriously called many elders to the east, in something called The Beckoning, the Sabbat have been especially responsive. Some elders are resisting the Beckoning.<br /> Sabbat reveling in the chaos and war of our times and is now seeking out the ancients to utterly destroy them. This may be what The Beckoning relates to. The Sabbat situation is unclear.<br /> Camarilla more secretive than ever and Masquerade strongly enforced.<br /> V5 playtest tomorrow with Mark Rein Hagen in the house to give a keynote address (taking all 5 of my 1st eds to be signed!)<br /> V5 beta test to be released soon after convention so everyone can try it<br /> Documentary on netflix next year (it was good, but I was genuinely upset that OP were not mentioned but V20 obviously was. They did address this in Q&amp;A, talking about an intended audience that is focused on drawing in totally new players and not having enough time to go into everything, but OP is an important part of the story, I mean 8 years without books and then they changed it in style)<br /> My white puppy rocked the house.<br /> <br /> Thats about all I can recall. If you have any burning questions, drop them here and ill try and get a response on the last day tomorrow.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Well, that's all terribly disappointing. Not surprising though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8975-macd21","name":"macd21","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T12:55:27-07:00","id":1091674,"title":"","content":"So will V20 and the other games still continue to be released, or is 5th edition the new and only direction? Because I'm not really digging much of what I'm seeing here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T13:58:18-07:00","id":1091693,"title":"","content":"A lot of what we've heard so far is going to be a matter of execution, so I'm reserving judgement. Bringing on Ken is pretty much the first truly smart thing WW has done so far, but it doesn't make up for a lot of other bad ideas.<br /> <br /> But what worries me the most?<br /> <br /> The &quot;50% of the profits&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, this is for the Storyteller's Vault material, not how they're going to treat hired freelancers (because no freelancer is going to take that deal).<br /> <br /> This is insanely exploitable. WWP puts in almost no work for their share of the profits, and can count any expense on their end managing the ST Vault as overhead no profit. If something is on the ST Vault for $5, the fans that made it don't get $2.50 every sale. That $5 is going to mostly get eaten up by credit card feeds, website and server costs, anything WW wants to claim as marking costs, anything WW wants to claim as costs to use of their IP, and easily drive down the final profit that gets divvied up to more like $0.50, leaving the content creators $0.25 a sale.<br /> <br /> There's a reason companies love royalty models, and creative content creators hate having to use them because companies are holding distribution as a bludgeon to keep creators into business models that are bad for them. It's how record companies profit from album sales while bands have to tour to actually make money, and how YouTube keeps their content providers in line. It's a model the promotes quantity over quality, because WWP will make money from all the sales even if no individual piece of content sells a lot, and WWP has to do almost no work at all.<br /> <br /> This also hurts freelancers because full professional supplements now have to compete with fan content. This means either less work because WWP will only work on the &quot;big&quot; projects like the core system and setting books (the 40 planned books sounds like a lot, but from the descriptions isn't that much when you consider their plans to make more smaller essential books, like a core V5 system book and at least three Sect books is already four planned books for what V20 does in one), or WWP will try to reduce their freelancer pay towards either royalties or to keep the price of professional books competitive with fan ST Vault books.<br /> <br /> 50% to the content creators sounds good, but it's the sort of thing that makes me nervous because it sounds good without guaranteeing anything.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T14:40:24-07:00","id":1091712,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091693#post1091693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of what we've heard so far is going to be a matter of execution, so I'm reserving judgement. Bringing on Ken is pretty much the first truly smart thing WW has done so far, but it doesn't make up for a lot of other bad ideas.<br /> <br /> But what worries me the most?<br /> <br /> The &quot;50% of the profits&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, this is for the Storyteller's Vault material, not how they're going to treat hired freelancers (because no freelancer is going to take that deal).<br /> <br /> This is insanely exploitable. WWP puts in almost no work for their share of the profits, and can count any expense on their end managing the ST Vault as overhead no profit. If something is on the ST Vault for $5, the fans that made it don't get $2.50 every sale. That $5 is going to mostly get eaten up by credit card feeds, website and server costs, anything WW wants to claim as marking costs, anything WW wants to claim as costs to use of their IP, and easily drive down the final profit that gets divvied up to more like $0.50, leaving the content creators $0.25 a sale.<br /> <br /> There's a reason companies love royalty models, and creative content creators hate having to use them because companies are holding distribution as a bludgeon to keep creators into business models that are bad for them. It's how record companies profit from album sales while bands have to tour to actually make money, and how YouTube keeps their content providers in line. It's a model the promotes quantity over quality, because WWP will make money from all the sales even if no individual piece of content sells a lot, and WWP has to do almost no work at all.<br /> <br /> This also hurts freelancers because full professional supplements now have to compete with fan content. This means either less work because WWP will only work on the &quot;big&quot; projects like the core system and setting books (the 40 planned books sounds like a lot, but from the descriptions isn't that much when you consider their plans to make more smaller essential books, like a core V5 system book and at least three Sect books is already four planned books for what V20 does in one), or WWP will try to reduce their freelancer pay towards either royalties or to keep the price of professional books competitive with fan ST Vault books.<br /> <br /> 50% to the content creators sounds good, but it's the sort of thing that makes me nervous because it sounds good without guaranteeing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Heavy- I don't think that the Hollywood model of expensing until there's no profits is the idea here. The idea is to encourage community creation, which ain't gonna happen if it's a ripoff. There are a bunch of functioning community content portals already rolling on DTRPG, and the 50% number seems to be derived from what is already working on them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5-richt","name":"RichT","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5_2.jpeg","title":"Onyx Path Creative Director","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:15:24-07:00","id":1091723,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091693#post1091693\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of what we've heard so far is going to be a matter of execution, so I'm reserving judgement. Bringing on Ken is pretty much the first truly smart thing WW has done so far, but it doesn't make up for a lot of other bad ideas.<br /> <br /> But what worries me the most?<br /> <br /> The &quot;50% of the profits&quot; thing.<br /> <br /> From what I understand, this is for the Storyteller's Vault material, not how they're going to treat hired freelancers (because no freelancer is going to take that deal).<br /> <br /> This is insanely exploitable. WWP puts in almost no work for their share of the profits, and can count any expense on their end managing the ST Vault as overhead no profit. If something is on the ST Vault for $5, the fans that made it don't get $2.50 every sale. That $5 is going to mostly get eaten up by credit card feeds, website and server costs, anything WW wants to claim as marking costs, anything WW wants to claim as costs to use of their IP, and easily drive down the final profit that gets divvied up to more like $0.50, leaving the content creators $0.25 a sale.<br /> <br /> There's a reason companies love royalty models, and creative content creators hate having to use them because companies are holding distribution as a bludgeon to keep creators into business models that are bad for them. It's how record companies profit from album sales while bands have to tour to actually make money, and how YouTube keeps their content providers in line. It's a model the promotes quantity over quality, because WWP will make money from all the sales even if no individual piece of content sells a lot, and WWP has to do almost no work at all.<br /> <br /> This also hurts freelancers because full professional supplements now have to compete with fan content. This means either less work because WWP will only work on the &quot;big&quot; projects like the core system and setting books (the 40 planned books sounds like a lot, but from the descriptions isn't that much when you consider their plans to make more smaller essential books, like a core V5 system book and at least three Sect books is already four planned books for what V20 does in one), or WWP will try to reduce their freelancer pay towards either royalties or to keep the price of professional books competitive with fan ST Vault books.<br /> <br /> 50% to the content creators sounds good, but it's the sort of thing that makes me nervous because it sounds good without guaranteeing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Wizards is doing the same thing with DM's Guild, that links to drivethroughrpg. The 50% is actually on the price of the product with no other cuts. It has a ton of contributors there and stuff from small companies. Also I would not worry about the professional supplements too much. Most people still will view it as good homebrew, but now you can reward good homebrewers with a few dollars, and have the all the works on an official site. At least if their model mirrors WotC.<br /> <br /> <br /> Edit: Yeah, I believe Richt is talking about the same thing, without mentioning names. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3669,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","user":"blackheartz","date":". 05-12-2017, 06:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3669-blackheartz","name":"blackheartz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3669_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T15:32:47-07:00","id":1091726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>RichT</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091712#post1091712\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Heavy- I don't think that the Hollywood model of expensing until there's no profits is the idea here. The idea is to encourage community creation, which ain't gonna happen if it's a ripoff. There are a bunch of functioning community content portals already rolling on DTRPG, and the 50% number seems to be derived from what is already working on them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Thanks for the insight on this, Rich. It's always good to see people who've been working in the industry for over two decades give their input with factual information. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":95,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","user":"Fat Larry","date":". 05-12-2017, 07:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T17:06:45-07:00","id":1091769,"title":"","content":"I wouldn't be surprised if DTRPG itself was involved in setting this up given that they already have the platform and have used it for D&amp;D. I have no inside knowledge, however. But as a vendor at DTRPG I will confirm that it's a gross split, with no weird accounting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Writer, Game Designer, Pro since 99.<br /> <br /> Thoughts at <a href=\"http://mobunited.com\" target=\"_blank\">mobunited.com</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/164-malcolm","name":"Malcolm","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar164_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T17:40:18-07:00","id":1091777,"title":"","content":"That's comforting. Though it then just puts the &quot;50%&quot; thing into a far less impressive claim, because it's just following what's already become an industry standard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T17:43:05-07:00","id":1091778,"title":"","content":"Read Werewolf Minds Theatre from By Night Studios. A lot of things are explained, it's 5th edition storyline.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091644#post1091644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ok, that's the reasonable approach. What if they truly realize that Gaia is dying? That what they're doing for a while just not working at all? Desperate times surged extremism through all of history.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Dunno, in my eyes, more reckless violence doesn't mean less desperation, it depends on the backstory.</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2809-batro","name":"batro","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"24"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T17:55:29-07:00","id":1091780,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2809-batro\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2809\" data-vbnamecard=\"2809\">batro</a> <br /> <br /> Except it's not? They've stated that their material is not being used for 5th Edition. Hell, there is no Second Impergium; there's an even BIGGER split, with the two groups within the Garou Nation, one who wants an impergium and one who feels that balance, or at least using the Weaver is not bad, existing. <br /> <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar741_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"741\" data-vbnamecard=\"741\">AnubisXy</a> <br /> <br /> I think it was said at one point that OPP could finish releasing the X20 stuff they have on the docket, but then they would not be directly developing any more OWoD stuff when 5th edition starts to drop. I can't find the quote, but I recall this being mentioned a couple of times.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T18:31:05-07:00","id":1091786,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091780#post1091780\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it was said at one point that OPP could finish releasing the X20 stuff they have on the docket, but then they would not be directly developing any more OWoD stuff when 5th edition starts to drop. I can't find the quote, but I recall this being mentioned a couple of times.</div> </div> </div> </div>Rich said in one of the Monday meeting notes after the buyout that WW would allow OP to honor all its kickstarter commitments and then reevaluate the situation moving forward (to paraphrase).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T19:04:29-07:00","id":1091797,"title":"","content":"Ok, watching the WW presentation right now, I thought I'll provide another summary after deejay's, so that's what I get from the first 17 minutes (I'll update this post as I progress):<br /> <br /> - every gaming format will get it's appropriate rulesets (good). Martin mentioned the difficulty of making it fresh, but upholding to the gravitas of the whole IP and it's fanbase. That's hopeful, at least they're fully aware of the conundrum.<br /> - the Sabbat is definitely away, doing something in the Middle East, but I don't think they're behind the wars, per se<br /> - new inqusition is an important thing but the source seems hidden so far<br /> - Martin dubbed it as &quot;welcome to the new Dark Ages&quot;, meaning that the global organizations are giving in and much more isolated city-states are the norm (hmmm... I'm undecided on this whole thing, it could end in a more flexible setting, but one of the main things which differentiated Masq from Requiem was the global organizations instead of isolated clusters and I hope it'll remain to an extent, although I'm not necessarily against some curbing back)<br /> - the Cam was forced to re-evaluate it's &quot;everyone in&quot; policy and effectively gave the streets to the Anarchs which are bound only by the 1st tradition, the Masquerade. Now, the Cam is more like an elite club, for which you'll get to be a member if you behave well and the main theme is &quot;the privileged few against the unwashed masses&quot;. He also mentioned neo-feudalism as a strong theme. (weeeeel... it certainly plays into the current zeitgeist, so it might help making it relevant to new gamers, which is good. I'm mostly okay with it, if executed well.)<br /> - the works of the art director lady seems good and she was in the same role during the MMO development and I liked those concept arts, so I really-really hope it'll be good. Obviously they're thinking that having a very strong visual identity is very important, which I can only nod and wait hopefully.<br /> <br /> - some more talk about the importance of visual identity by Carl. In the age of surveillance, Masquerade is even more critical and vampires have two visual identities, one &quot;for the street&quot; and one for elysium, when they can revel in their monstrous nature (so no changeling-like). Hmmm, vampire dress-up parties? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Okay, aside from kidding, that actually sounds cool and makes sense.<br /> -Mary Lee just started to speak about more of the above, starting with the clans, showing sneak peeks. They're good, very good, dark and evocative. Yes, much of it will be photography, but I like what I seen this far. I'll ever miss the look of the old books, but it could be good with this style and level of quality. Less like &quot;gothic comics&quot; (again, I loved that style) and more like a modern dark photography-portfolio. (although I'm not sure how they imagine the photography-centered art direction in the case of the more fantastic lines, like Werewolf or Changeling...)<br /> <br /> System talk by Karim:<br /> <br /> - aside from what we already know, he actually mentioned the ideal possibility of satisfying many different gaming styles, from freeform/diceless to adding many layers of detail. (this could be good, if implemented successfully, I'd love it, but I'm not sure how they want to do it. WotC promised the same high-modularity with D&amp;D 5e and not quite delivered it at the end. Still, I'd be okay with a simplistic core, if, for example a more detailed &quot;combat handbook&quot; will follow.)<br /> - dots remain (it's good, it's easy), d10s remain (people love d10, possibility of custom d10s)<br /> - quite possibly fixed target numbers, counting number of successes for level of success (okay with that. Fiddling with TN has it's merits, it's flexible and gradual, but NWoD and SR 4e-5e went for the fixed TN for a reason)<br /> - simpler conflict resolution, ideally with 1 roll<br /> - should be 90% percent compatibility with statblocks in the old books, new people should understand those easily, or play by the old rules if you like and using statblocks from the new books<br /> -I'm actually started to be getting sold on the new hunger mechanic's concept. It's more risk-management than resource management, which is good, though I'm still not sure how you suppose to fuel supernatural powers this way.<br /> -they seem to wanting to go with it to a narrative direction, &quot;incorporating 21st century game design&quot; and &quot;making the game something which is recognizable, but feels like it was made in 2017&quot;. Martin talked about player agency. Oooookay. I seen it coming and I'm not exactly that happy on this, but they said the amount of that is still a question, so we'll see.<br /> <br /> Q&amp;A:<br /> <br /> - Corebook will only have the core 7 clans (or no clans, just rules and the Cam book will have those? I'm not sure, but might be, since they'll coming out simultaneously). Anarch book will have thin-bloods. I guess the Sabbat clans will come with the later Sabbat book. Independents will come later too, probably. Hmph. Not my favorite idea, those clans are staple of the setting. How they intend to do Europe without the Giovanni, the Tzimisce? I somewhat fear that the reason might be that they aren't figured out how to sync those clans with the new rules systems (however, the core 7 has the Tremere, so it might be also just their plans for the metaplot), like we discussed in earlier threads about the &quot;you are what you eat&quot; thing (which curiously didn't get mentioned so far).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-13-2017, 01:04 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-12T23:50:13-07:00","id":1091847,"title":"","content":"The first (only?) video from WoD Berlin that I've seen posted so far:<br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yvwroDSLO3E\" target=\"_blank\">World of Darkness Berlin - Vampire the Masquerade 5th Edition Presentation</a><br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yvwroDSLO3E\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yvwroDSLO3E\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yvwroDSLO3E\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=yvwroDSLO3E </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">- Arthur &quot;Torakhan&quot; Dreese <span style=\"color:silver\"><b>David &quot;Wall-of-Text&quot; Tealdeer</b> - US2012070036\u200b - Grand Rapids, MI</span><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img855/1250/jv8k.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nmeqe3m\" target=\"_blank\">V:tM 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/pavtnjj\" target=\"_blank\">Hunters Hunted II</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/l3hjgjt\" target=\"_blank\">Anarchs Unbound</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/mxyvsy9\" target=\"_blank\">W:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/k5qe4j4\" target=\"_blank\">W20 Changing Breeds</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/m64m9o5\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3rd Edition</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/qxkop7m\" target=\"_blank\">M:tA 20th</a> \u2022 <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/nd6kms2\" target=\"_blank\">W20BotW</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/780-torakhan","name":"Torakhan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar780_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"576"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T00:02:12-07:00","id":1091852,"title":"","content":"The &quot;street identity&quot; and &quot;Elysium identity&quot; is also another point where V5 seems to be moving closer to Requiem in a fashion that might make them more blurry than the two very distinct games as they stood with V20 vs. VtR 2e. In VtR 2e, instead of Virtues and Vices, vampires have Masks (the face they show humans) and Dirges (the face they show other vampires).<br /> <br /> I'm not super worried about that, but it does feel a bit strange to hear that V5 is going to be more VtR like after all the work put into VtR 2e to try to differentiate it from VtM.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T01:39:51-07:00","id":1091868,"title":"","content":"So how does OPP fit into all this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T02:20:27-07:00","id":1091876,"title":"","content":"After watching the video? Doesn't really seem like they do. Martin seemed to dodge the question on further 20th books after the current slate are finished (though partially implied the keynote address that's going on now might give details on that.. or not and that was meant for other questions), and it seems pretty clear they have no intention of hiring OPP to do any of the work on the 5e books directly.<br /> <br /> They were a lot better than some of the past things about acknowledging OPP in carrying the WoD to this point, but they still seem pretty set on taking the WoD and running their own way with it; implying OPP will phase more and more towards just handling the CofD and Exalted for them.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T03:59:23-07:00","id":1091887,"title":"","content":"50% is actually pretty low... Valve gets 75% from cosmetics, tournaments etc. in Dota and other games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T04:20:59-07:00","id":1091889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091777#post1091777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's comforting. Though it then just puts the &amp;quot;50%&amp;quot; thing into a far less impressive claim, because it's just following what's already become an industry standard.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's still very new ground for WW. They don't have the history of supporting third party/fan content that D&amp;d does. <br /> <br /> I thought Changeling was one of the big five? Are they counting Mummy the Cursed? I think everyone would prefer a new Changeling game before a new Mummy game. <br /> <br /> The other four being Vampire Werewolf Mage and Wraith of course.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3075-coridan","name":"Coridan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3075_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"528"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T05:19:13-07:00","id":1091902,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091868#post1091868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how does OPP fit into all this?</div> </div> </div> </div>At this moment, they publishing Beckett's Jyhad Diary, the centerpiece of bringing in the metaplot to the current day and age.<br /> After that, they will probably not work on the main book of VtM, but as far as I gathered, WW is not going to be doing a lot of the books themselves.<br /> <br /> And in regards to the second Imperigium.<br /> <br /> We've had two slides and a piece of flavor text. Let's just chill for a moment.<br /> <br /> [/Growls, who is currently sitting in Berlin, awaiting to go to the V5 playtest]","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T07:33:25-07:00","id":1091938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091902#post1091902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At this moment, they publishing Beckett's Jyhad Diary, the centerpiece of bringing in the metaplot to the current day and age.<br /> After that, they will probably not work on the main book of VtM, but as far as I gathered, WW is not going to be doing a lot of the books themselves.<br /> <br /> And in regards to the second Imperigium.<br /> <br /> We've had two slides and a piece of flavor text. Let's just chill for a moment.<br /> <br /> [/Growls, who is currently sitting in Berlin, awaiting to go to the V5 playtest]</div> </div> </div> </div>The term &quot;2nd Impergium&quot; remains incredibly incongruous with the setting lore established thus far, so you can't really wriggle very far out from that rock.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T08:25:39-07:00","id":1091958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Growls</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091902#post1091902\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <br /> We've had two slides and a piece of flavor text. Let's just chill for a moment.<br /> <br /> [/Growls, who is currently sitting in Berlin, awaiting to go to the V5 playtest]</div> </div> </div> </div>Too late for that, I'd say. You've still got the same people saying the same thing over the last few months like a broken record. Former OP writers are spreading incorrect info on social media that are utterly false. It's just a wildfire, created by the same people, fueled by the same people, that simply won't stop for whatever reasons. We've got so little info, yet former OP writers are already telling you to avoid it, because Ken Hite is a priviliged white male. It's all over Facebook. <br /> <br /> If the bitter meter weren't already broken, I'd sure as shit say it is now. I've definitely seen some new (and valid) reasons for wanting to avoid V5, like Darksiders for example, but he's sure as shit in the minority.<br /> <br /> A LOT of this crap is coming off as sour grapes, while Paradox couldn't care less about the same forum posters and people on facebook that are already swearing it off. The money is in the videogames, which are coming regardless.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T09:31:30-07:00","id":1091981,"title":"","content":"Going back to what Karim said about the Hunger mechanics, after sleeping on it, I have a few more points I'd like to be addressed:<br /> <br /> - How is it working with disciplines, blood buffing, healing, etc?<br /> - He said that a gas meter isn't sexy. Ok, I'm willing to buy into a new, more evocative mechanic, but what he said about Composure, it's just another gas meter, another resource.<br /> - As for Composure... Now are we going to have two different stats of, essentially &quot;keeping it cool&quot;? Because WP already has that role and it is a thing from the very beginning. I'd prefer integrating it to the new mechanics to adding a second, rather similar stat. I think it's counterintuitive, especially for new players.<br /> <br /> <br /> Sabbat metaplot: giving it a second thought, I don't have problems for the Sabbat digging like mad on the Middle East, using the wars as a cover, but what the Assamites thinking about it? I really hope they don't want to put the independents totally on the bench. Also, I have problems with the sect, which keeps individual freedom at the upmost importance in their worldview taking an en masse, ehm, <i>Sabbatical</i>, leaving behind all their territories and interests. Also, would the Tzimisce elders really leave their ancient East European strongholds? I think not.<br /> <br /> So, much to answer here, and they'll need <i>very good and convincing </i>answers, IMO, if they don't want to alienate a very big chunk of the fanbase.<br /> <br /> <br /> As for the Requieminizing of the game, it's interesting. It definitely seems like they want to take some steps into that direction. I'm not sure how I feel about it, I don't want the setting to lose it's identity, I kept with it for a reason, but some loosening up and integrating some concepts might be good. I want the game to move forward, I just fear it'll lose itself in the process, but I hope not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T11:52:41-07:00","id":1092023,"title":"","content":"Finished surprise ST-ing a V5 playtest a little bit ago. Will put up my thoughts later. First impressions are good, though not everybody is going to like it. That said, they emphasized repeatedly that the playtest rules are barely even an alpha version. Nothing is locked in at this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T11:55:08-07:00","id":1092025,"title":"","content":"No rage? So .... When will You Lost your composure? I've already finished new werewolf novel. And afer that... Reading news from Berlin. Just don't belive this. Hope OnyxPath will be releasing their stuff. If allowed... Hey! Give us Some info bout playtesting","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T11:59:26-07:00","id":1092028,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092023#post1092023\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Finished surprise ST-ing a V5 playtest a little bit ago. Will put up my thoughts later. First impressions are good, though not everybody is going to like it. That said, they emphasized repeatedly that the playtest rules are barely even an alpha version. Nothing is locked in at this point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would still love to hear your input and thoughts though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-13T12:05:41-07:00","id":1092032,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092025#post1092025\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No rage? So .... When will You Lost your composure? I've already finished new werewolf novel. And afer that... Reading news from Berlin. Just don't belive this. Hope OnyxPath will be releasing their stuff. If allowed... Hey! Give us Some info bout playtesting</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> There will be Rage. Calm down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"