":"Very enjoyable convention! I had a lot of fun and some very interesting conversations about the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T01:01:11-07:00","id":1092263,"title":"","content":"That was a great experience, I made quite a few international contacts and even LARPed for the first time ever.<br /> <br /> If you anyone is interested, Darker Days Radio live blogged the event, with tons of info, recordings of keynotes, and even a live streamed episode. <a href=\"http://www.beastsofwar.com/eventslist/world-of-darkness-berlin-live-blog/\" target=\"_blank\">http://www.beastsofwar.com/eventslis...lin-live-blog/</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T08:10:19-07:00","id":1092333,"title":"","content":"I think maybe there's a little too much effort in aligning The game world politics to real world politics.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T13:59:03-07:00","id":1092477,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> : dont keep us sitting on needles, dude <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, what's with this &quot;the Sabbat is off in the Middle East&quot; thing? Does that mean that the continental US and Mexico are now boring Cammarilla territory?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-14T15:56:29-07:00","id":1092559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092477#post1092477\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> : dont keep us sitting on needles, dude <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Also, what's with this &quot;the Sabbat is off in the Middle East&quot; thing? Does that mean that the continental US and Mexico are now boring Cammarilla territory?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> This is conjecture, but I assume there are still plenty of Sabbat in North America. It's just that there's sooooo many elders heading to the Middle East that Sabbat activity is focused there right now. To, y'know, diablerize all of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://darker-days.org/\" target=\"_blank\">Darker Days Radio</a> - The World of Darkness Podcast<br /> <a href=\"http://historylessons.libsyn.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Unbuttoned History</a> - A History Podcast with Jokes","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/124-darker-days-mike","name":"Darker Days Mike","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar124_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"134"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T00:08:27-07:00","id":1092679,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darker Days Mike</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092559#post1092559\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> This is conjecture, but I assume there are still plenty of Sabbat in North America. It's just that there's sooooo many elders heading to the Middle East that Sabbat activity is focused there right now. To, y'know, diablerize all of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>That is a sensible assumption.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><span style=\"color:#000080\">Matthew Dawkins</span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000080\">In-House Developer for Onyx Path Publishing</span></b><br /> <br /> <i><span style=\"font-family:arial\"><b><span style=\"color:#008080\">Website: </span><a href=\"http://www.matthewdawkins.com\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.matthewdawkins.com</span></a><br /> <span style=\"color:#008080\">Patreon: </span><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins\" target=\"_blank\"><span style=\"color:#008080\">https://www.patreon.com/matthewdawkins</span></a></b></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/152-the-gentleman-gamer","name":"The Gentleman Gamer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar152_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1698"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T03:03:42-07:00","id":1092713,"title":"","content":"Any words from testers about mechanic changes? First impressions about glimpses of setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T03:32:53-07:00","id":1092721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Torakhan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1091847#post1091847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The first (only?) video from WoD Berlin that I've seen posted so far:</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> thats me with my dog!! thanks for posting!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T03:58:49-07:00","id":1092728,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>werewolf43</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092713#post1092713\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any words from testers about mechanic changes? First impressions about glimpses of setting?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Yes. Lots, where to begin? I know<br /> <br /> ALL OF THIS IS SUBJECT TO CHANGE IN THE FINAL PRODUCT<br /> <br /> Only 3 Attributes - Physical, Social and Mental, 1-5 dots<br /> Specialities for these Attributes like Strength, Charisma etc (the old atts) and others that were not old Atts add one die<br /> Skills pretty much unchanged 1-5 dots<br /> TN nearly always 6<br /> Difficulty is now number of succs. needed<br /> Disciplines are activated by &quot;Rousing the Blood&quot;<br /> This means you add all your (red) Hunger die to the pool (they replace ordinary die). We started with 1 die.<br /> Hunger die only added to skill based pools (including pools that use skills for disciplines) but not others like willpower.<br /> Hunger die track 1-5<br /> Hunger increased during play, but it happened to me only once and I cant recall the mechanical cause<br /> Hunger went to zero when someone fed<br /> Victims sometimes gave a small bonus to trait rolls (eg. the homeless guy gave a die for the next stealth roll I think). This was even when partially drained.<br /> Each 1 on Hunger die triggers a Compulsion<br /> Compulsions are clan based and the consequences situation based and were randomly generated. Our hungry Toreador walked into a burned out haven and became entranced by the beauty of the destruction. Police then crept up on him.<br /> Compulsions could be overcome with Composure, but this left you with less Compusure to counter with should a Frenzy occur later.<br /> Frenzy occurred when more 1s came up together (I think)<br /> Willpower was 1-5 and could be spent to reroll all the failed dice, so long as there was at least one success<br /> Humanity was in there at 1-10, but was not tested or afaik used in the beta, the focus was on other mechanics<br /> Characters also had advantages like backgounds and merits, but these too were not a focus of play<br /> The focus was really on how the mechanics and storytelling aspects of play integrated with one another<br /> Im not going to give my views as I want that to brew for a while and to submit it to the offical feedback place first<br /> The story was very dense - I dont think any table completed it in the 4 hours of play - and was a direct follow up to the events of the Enlightenment in Blood LARP which concluded the night before. The story became the first event of the new VtM metaplot.<br /> It was set in Berlin in the current nights during an Anarch uprising that saw the final death of Breidenstein and numerous other vampires as well as follow up trouble coming from the Inquisition. We were all Camarilla neonates trying to find the vampire who had blood bonded us all. It was a clusterfuck. There were several classic moments in the story where the Hunger mechanics produced a genuine 'Vampire' moment.<br /> <br /> I made one reporting error in my earlier post, the Anarchs are being forced out of the Camarilla, of course. But its a changed Camarilla, almost broken. The Anarchs are basically turning on a tyrannical, despotic organisation. The events in Berlin were the catalyst for a global change, as the Anarchs pulled the Camarilla to its knees here last week.<br /> Generation was still in development but the idea talked about was that it would be less discernable and more difficult to know which generation your character or anothers actually was. Line of descent may be growing murky to the characters.<br /> Gehenna (the actual events of any ToJ metaplot) was not revealed but my sense is that V5 will feature a selection of elements from ToJ blended togther into a new version of Gehenna which for now we only know as the Gehenna Wars.<br /> The two looks for vampire I mentioned are cosmetic looks, nothing more. Vampires in Elysium dress (and act) differently. This I feel is a nod to the LARPers, who like to really go to town on a look that would often shred the Masquerade on the streets. Elysium is now a place where they can let their monsters show and relax.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-15-2017, 07:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T04:06:44-07:00","id":1092730,"title":"","content":"Thank You! Hmmm I see big changes at the moment. We shall see final product. Was there any combat scenes? If Yes, what's Your opinion?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T04:20:49-07:00","id":1092732,"title":"","content":"on combat - oh yeah! mostly between the characters as the situation was really intensive and desperate.<br /> You could rouse the blood to increase any Attribute not just Physical. Also to heal.<br /> Damage was really interesting, it came as either Superficial or Aggravated. Anything that could conceivably kill you was Aggravated for you. Aggravated damage was also very slow to heal.<br /> You didnt take any penalty or injury until a certain level was reached (5 I think) then you took a nasty consequence that was dependent on the type of damage used.<br /> The fighting was between the coterie members, the coterie and the German armed forces, the coterie and some very well equipped dudes who were likely New Inquisitors, and the coterie and some Anarchs. It worked well and was entertaining.<br /> By the way, a little bird sitting in the middle of the nest told me that EDOM from Nights Black Agents were being ported or adapted into WoD...check out The Dracula Dossier for more on that little insight...and you'll realise this could easily be and probably will be part or even the heart of the New Inquisition.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-15-2017, 07:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T04:42:07-07:00","id":1092737,"title":"","content":"Wait, you were fighting the German Armed Forces? <i>Why?</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5307-loomer","name":"loomer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5307_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"661"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T04:46:27-07:00","id":1092739,"title":"","content":"There was media reporting about major terrorist attacks after exploding vans were driven into several vampire havens. To be honest, we had no idea who they were, they were just flying in with helicopters and spreading out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-15-2017, 07:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T04:59:55-07:00","id":1092742,"title":"","content":"I'm still at the airport in Germany but I figure I'll add my own two cents to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2157_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2157\" data-vbnamecard=\"2157\">deejay</a> has posted. I'm not going to get too hung up on system minutiae as that's the most likely thing to change going forward. Instead I'll focusing more on mechanical concepts and applications. <br /> <br /> The &quot;big thing&quot; that it seemed like this was a testbed for is the Hunger system as a replacement for Blood Points. The basic idea is that rather than decreasing the amount of blood you have you increase the amount of hunger you have. Rather than spending Blood Points you instead &quot;Rouse the Blood&quot; to accomplish a variety of things (basically all the same things you spend blood for under the current rules). A few subtle but important inclusions are that you must Rouse the Blood to awaken each night, any vampire must Rouse in order to not appear dead, and all uses of Disciplines require Rousing. You keep track of how many times you Rouse the Blood in a scene and at the end of that scene you roll that many dice. Any dice that don't roll a success add to your Hunger (a scale of 1-5). Any time you make a skill roll or skill-based Discipline roll you have a number of dice in your pool replaced by &quot;Hunger dice,&quot; equal to your Hunger rating. These dice function like normal dice and can contribute successes, but if any of them roll a 1 you gain a temporary Compulsion from your Beast (note that 1s do not subtract from successes in these rules so you aren't getting double-whammied or anything). Compulsions are tics of your predatory vampiric nature that can vary in severity depending on the number of Hunger dice that rolled a 1. In the game I ran a Toreador was overwhelmed with strong emotion for someone in the scene, a Ventrue felt compelled to assert his dominance and leadership over the group, and another Ventrue felt incredible anxiety at the lack of order and structure they had without guidance from their superiors. These were all pretty minor Compulsions and we didn't have anyone fail badly enough to pull one of the nastier ones (though one character was walking around with 4 Hunger for a bit). <br /> Hunger is reduced by feeding, shock of all shocks. There was a scale that told you how much Hunger was removed by feeding on what. IIRC animals removed 2 and feeding on a human without killing them removed 3. Feeding on a human and killing them in the process removes 4 and is also the only way to reduce your Hunger below 1 (temporarily), otherwise all vampires are assumed to always have at least 1 Hunger. <br /> Honestly, it worked pretty well and everyone I talked to seemed to feel likewise. It needs refinement, something even Karim said in a couple conversations I had with him, but the core concept and system is actually surprisingly thematic and functional. <br /> <br /> In this set of rules the extent of &quot;you are what you eat&quot; was getting small, temporary bonuses from feeding on certain people. They said this is something they want to continue with but are still developing a proper system for. At this point though assuming the final system for that has broadly similar outcomes to the listed effects in the playtest it <i>doesn't</i> seem like that addition to the system is going to be as huge and game-changing as some people were thinking. <br /> <br /> The other addition that was generally a hit (with exceptions I'll talk about) was &quot;Success With Consequences,&quot; wherein if the number of successes you rolled fell exactly one short of the number you needed you could choose to succeed but have the ST add in some complication or consequence. It only happened a couple times at my table and worked well both times. Other people I talked to reported similarly with the exception of one table where it apparently happened so often it became cumbersome to the flow. Seems like something that depends a great deal on the fall of the dice and the kinds of things the ST decides to throw in. <br /> <br /> There are other smaller things I could go into, but deejay already mostly touched on them and I feel they're fairly minor details to really heavily scrutinize at this early stage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:14:11-07:00","id":1092748,"title":"","content":"Well.<br /> The table I ran had a player death. Turns out a frenzy-struck vampire versus a team of GSG9 with assault rifles on FA is pretty detrimental to anyone.<br /> <br /> I was a Storyteller, and I really enjoyed to see my player's cringe when the Ventrue realized that a baby was an amazing meal to get her hands on. I loved the fact that the writers decided to give each of them names, and focus on the visceral side of the hunt.<br /> <br /> As far as I gathered, the Success with Consequence is an option, not a requirement, and only available when the ST deems that it can actually happen. It shouldn't draw attention away from the game. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2157_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2157\" data-vbnamecard=\"2157\">deejay</a> (who I also had the pleasure of running a VtM game for on thursday) did cover the basics, so I got nothing more to add, but can answer for anyone needing to learn about how it was to be running it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>__________________________________________________ </b><br /> <span style=\"font-family:times new roman\"><b><i>Preaching the enlightened gospels of Gaming Anarchy</i></b></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls","name":"Growls","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar225_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"292"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:27:51-07:00","id":1092753,"title":"","content":"I'm WtA Gm and my group won't let me become player sadly, so I'm very interested in tools GM will get in upcoming WoD games, in game mastering aspects so ... please, feel invited to tell more about how it was running the game.<br /> I imagine You get sheets of GSG9 assault force. Combined to players (one died) what was the difference between V5 vampire fighting soldiers and V&lt;5 (V20 for example).<br /> Did You feel that player characters manifesting their ,,curses&quot; (Toreador and ruined place) were well combined with game mechanics? - not just a roleplay, but simply enforced by game?<br /> Could You tell who won the fight GSG9 or players? And how it looked?<br /> Thanks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1784,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","user":"werewolf43","date":". 05-15-2017, 08:33 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T05:56:51-07:00","id":1092763,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092728#post1092728\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Only 3 Attributes - Physical, Social and Mental, 1-5 dots<br /> Specialities for these Attributes like Strength, Charisma etc (the old atts) and others that were not old Atts add one die</div> </div> </div> </div>At first glance I like this kind of streamlining - less micromanagement of the base stats.<br /> But on the second thought, and ironically from a *roleplay* perspective...it gives you less options, stat-wise.<br /> <br /> Namely, you could previously play a scrawny, thin character that, however, was nimble and swift. Or a character with a high stamina and strength, that had the dexterity of a brick - the hulking giant type.<br /> And whatever combinations and reasons you can come up with, really.<br /> <br /> Now with only the 'physical' attribute, everybody who's a very good runner or a nimble pickpocket can also benchpress a literal benchful of people. For..some reason. A person that is good at socializing also looks great? An intelligent person also has the bestest perception?<br /> As much as the system streamlines numbers juggling for the sake of RP, it also limits the different possibilities for rolls. Heh.<br /> And yes, I fully realize a player could voluntarily decide to use less dice on a roll where they imagine their character'd be less developed physically, but..the majority of players probably won't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 05-15-2017, 09:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T06:07:47-07:00","id":1092768,"title":"","content":"Ambrosia, this is exactly what my table bought up, and it was taken on board for consideration with gratitude. We suggested refining characters Attributes with more specialisations (we only had 1 each) and with some that also included things we were weaker at. Karim also told me that the 3 attribuite system will likely change in some important ways. <br /> Justin Achillis keynote speech on why we play games taught me the most important thing I learned at the conference. His claim that it was the most important thing Ill ever learn may turn oiut to be true too. I hope that presentation gets put up somewhere. <br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/225-growls\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar225_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"225\" data-vbnamecard=\"225\">Growls</a> thank you for the game on Thursday! Glad to match you to an account here! What was your favourite thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-15-2017, 09:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T07:05:39-07:00","id":1092789,"title":"","content":"Of note, the Attributes with Specializations and Superficial/Aggravated Damage types is lifted directly from MET VtM.<br /> <br /> In MET VtM, the specializations function to define a character in 'what they're best at' and grant bonuses to tasks when those would come into play, both from a bonus to a dice pool and other bonuses. A Strength focused character would get a situational +3 bonus to their Physical when raw strength (not combat!) would be useful, or bonuses from Disciplines. A Stamina focused character ignores wound penalties. All of this could be fine in TT. We'll have to see what the specializations actually DO in practice.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 05-15-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T07:37:03-07:00","id":1092798,"title":"","content":"I must say, I'm a lot more positive than two pages ago. Although seeing LARP rulesets backtranslated into PnP leaves me somewhat worried. But I've gone from &quot;buy on a sale&quot; to &quot;buy after a year&quot;.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092768#post1092768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Justin Achillis keynote speech on why we play games taught me the most important thing I learned at the conference. His claim that it was the most important thing Ill ever learn may turn oiut to be true too. I hope that presentation gets put up somewhere.</div> </div> </div> </div>Could we get a cliffnotes version, please?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T08:16:48-07:00","id":1092816,"title":"","content":"His talk was about the impact of Self Determination Theory on game design and the understanding of why we play games. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-determination_theory\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/9/9e/Greek_uc_psi_icon.svg/1280px-Greek_uc_psi_icon.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=index&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-determination_theory\" target=\"_blank\"> Self-determination theory - Wikipedia </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-determination_theory\" target=\"_blank\"> https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-determination_theory </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> He talked about the ways in which autonomy, mastery and relatedness matter in our games, and what we can do with this. Since I believe this talk will be put up soon enough, I wont spoil any more. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T08:21:37-07:00","id":1092817,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2157_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2157\" data-vbnamecard=\"2157\">deejay</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> . Thank you. I've gone one question if you don't mind: if there was a list of compulsions,could you tell me what were the ones for the nosferatu clan?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T08:42:51-07:00","id":1092826,"title":"","content":"I am more cautiously optimistic about everything now, though the scenario being 'SUDDENLY TERRORISTS!' is a little disturbing, but I get what they were wanting to accomplish with it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T11:23:16-07:00","id":1092882,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092817#post1092817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thank you. I've gone one question if you don't mind: if there was a list of compulsions,could you tell me what were the ones for the nosferatu clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>I played a Ventrue, but all the potential compulsions were in the document they handed out (and took back). Each clan had about 3. I cannot remember what those were, sorry, but someone who played Nosferatu might. When WWP release the (probably tweaked) beta test rules, you will know.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T11:30:47-07:00","id":1092887,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092826#post1092826\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I am more cautiously optimistic about everything now, though the scenario being 'SUDDENLY TERRORISTS!' is a little disturbing, but I get what they were wanting to accomplish with it.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> It was more &quot;SUDDENLY ANARCHS!&quot; with the terror attacks (and some mobile phone network blackouts) being blamed on terrorism. This struck me as a classic WoD approach. It is just a very touchy subject, but ignoring or underplaying its presence in our world would have been cowardly and skewed. They balanced its presentation well, at least my tables ST did. I would have loved to listen in on the table with Mark Rein Hagen as player and Justin Achilli as ST (I think thats what was going on there!)<br /> The situatation seems to be the Sabbat dabbled in the Middle East, playing all sides, and that this meddling kicked off the 2nd Inquisition, which in turn led to a night in Berlin in which careless Berlin Anarchs had messages intercepted by this Inquisition, leading to the catastrophic events of last Friday night here and the eventual expulsion of Anarchs from the Camarilla and its setup as a &quot;closed room&quot;, a secret society you have to be invited into.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-15-2017, 02:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T11:46:20-07:00","id":1092890,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092887#post1092887\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> It was more &quot;SUDDENLY ANARCHS!&quot; with the terror attacks (and some mobile phone network blackouts) being blamed on terrorism. This struck me as a classic WoD approach. It is just a very touchy subject, but ignoring or underplaying its presence in our world would have been cowardly and skewed. They balanced its presentation well, at least my tables ST did. I would have loved to listen in on the table with Mark Rein Hagen as player and Justin Achilli as ST (I think thats what was going on there!)<br /> The situatation seems to be the Sabbat dabbled in the Middle East, playing all sides, and that this meddling kicked off the 2nd Inquisition, which in turn led to a night in Berlin in which careless Berlin Anarchs had messages intercepted by this Inquisition, leading to the catastrophic events of last Friday night here and the eventual expulsion of Anarchs from the Camarilla and its setup as a &quot;closed room&quot;, a secret society you have to be invited into.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> On no, I get that it's a cover. Our local LARP ended up having some shenanigans go down that brought in Project Twilight on the blaming of a bombing as a terrorist group, so I get that it's a standard cover. I am slightly sick, so I guess I didn't articulate that well enough. Still, cautiously optimistic. If nothing else, most of the group I play with seems to really like the concept of Hunger, so they've managed to convince some fickle people who don't like change... to like change...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1808,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","user":"elmerg","date":". 05-15-2017, 02:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T11:49:27-07:00","id":1092892,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092882#post1092882\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I played a Ventrue, but all the potential compulsions were in the document they handed out (and took back). Each clan had about 3. I cannot remember what those were, sorry, but someone who played Nosferatu might. When WWP release the (probably tweaked) beta test rules, you will know.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks anyway","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:10:41-07:00","id":1092899,"title":"","content":"Do you know (the you being those who attended) is this &quot;Convention LARPs influence metaplot&quot; thing is going to be a more permanent way of moving the metaplot forward?<br /> On one hand, I fully approve of integrating at least part of the community into the metaplot, on the other hand, LARPs can get ridiculously out of hand. Perhaps some sort of crowd-sourced tournament could be made for the TT players, like how GW handled the Storm Of Chaos (only, you know, good).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:21:03-07:00","id":1092905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092899#post1092899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know (the you being those who attended) is this &quot;Convention LARPs influence metaplot&quot; thing is going to be a more permanent way of moving the metaplot forward?<br /> On one hand, I fully approve of integrating at least part of the community into the metaplot, on the other hand, LARPs can get ridiculously out of hand. Perhaps some sort of crowd-sourced tournament could be made for the TT players, like how GW handled the Storm Of Chaos (only, you know, good).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Not one of the guys there, but they talked in the video on youtube about collating info from a lot of sources, specifically mentioning the video games they plan to release as well. So they probably will mine from a lot of sources, with the LARPs being the 'here's the enaction of what we plan'. Because all of the situations with that LARP sound very scripted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:30:00-07:00","id":1092910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092899#post1092899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do you know (the you being those who attended) is this &quot;Convention LARPs influence metaplot&quot; thing is going to be a more permanent way of moving the metaplot forward?<br /> On one hand, I fully approve of integrating at least part of the community into the metaplot, on the other hand, LARPs can get ridiculously out of hand. Perhaps some sort of crowd-sourced tournament could be made for the TT players, like how GW handled the Storm Of Chaos (only, you know, good).</div> </div> </div> </div>For some reason I feel like this approach is fraught with the potential for gonzo aburdity. How does it occur to anyone that the ego-driven, interpersonal histrionics of individual LARPers is equal to having talented, professional writers writing a compelling story and materials.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:44:24-07:00","id":1092917,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092910#post1092910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason I feel like this approach is fraught with the potential for gonzo aburdity. How does it occur to anyone that the ego-driven, interpersonal histrionics of individual LARPers is equal to having talented, professional writers writing a compelling story and materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey now. It could work, if you go with a scenario-based approach to LARPing. nWW releases LARP module X to the wider community (1WbN, most likely), waits a few months for the module to be run, collects outcomes, metaplot moves forward.<br /> <br /> While I am as wary of LARP shennenigans as you are, not all of us are histrionic munchkin snowflakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T12:48:31-07:00","id":1092920,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092917#post1092917\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hey now. It could work, if you go with a scenario-based approach to LARPing. nWW releases LARP module X to the wider community (1WbN, most likely), waits a few months for the module to be run, collects outcomes, metaplot moves forward.<br /> <br /> While I am as wary of LARP shennenigans as you are, not all of us are histrionic munchkin snowflakes.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If anything, any LARPs that factor their input into the metaplot will be done internally by WW at conventions or WW-run events. The LARP organizations would have to redo their ENTIRE structure to accommodate any 'the stuff we do defines the metaplot'.<br /> <br /> OWbN has no plans to reset, their internal metaplot has been going for 20+ years, they still use Laws of the Night. The Mind's Eye Society is not beholden to use the material as presented (as exampled by the current chronicle they're planning which adapts the By Night Studios setting, the chronicle that just ended was another 'Let's run Revised!' chronicle. The other groups are small enough that I never see any talk about them any more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T13:17:57-07:00","id":1092927,"title":"","content":"First off, thank all of you for the info, it's greatly appreciated!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092763#post1092763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At first glance I like this kind of streamlining - less micromanagement of the base stats.<br /> But on the second thought, and ironically from a *roleplay* perspective...it gives you less options, stat-wise.<br /> <br /> Namely, you could previously play a scrawny, thin character that, however, was nimble and swift. Or a character with a high stamina and strength, that had the dexterity of a brick - the hulking giant type.<br /> And whatever combinations and reasons you can come up with, really.<br /> <br /> Now with only the 'physical' attribute, everybody who's a very good runner or a nimble pickpocket can also benchpress a literal benchful of people. For..some reason. A person that is good at socializing also looks great? An intelligent person also has the bestest perception?<br /> As much as the system streamlines numbers juggling for the sake of RP, it also limits the different possibilities for rolls. Heh.<br /> And yes, I fully realize a player could voluntarily decide to use less dice on a roll where they imagine their character'd be less developed physically, but..the majority of players probably won't.</div> </div> </div> </div>That was my exact thought since I saw the BNS rules. It's easier to track in a LARP environment than the traditional 9 atrrs, but unnecessarily restrictive for tabletop. I'm glad it'll get refined, let's hope for the best!<br /> <br /> Anyway, all of the other things seems actually quite good! I'm very happy they took this approach with you are what you eat instead of the more extreme ones. This one could add to the flavor of the game without constraining it and I always said something like that would be okay. The TN/required successes are going to the direction of Shadowrun's recent editions, I'm perfectly okay with that.<br /> <br /> The Hunger mechanics seems to require a bit more bookkeeping than ideal at first glance (and I still think it's a little too much to have essentially two WP stat to track) but I could imagine that it is worse in paper than in practice and overall, it seems good and quite flavorful and dare I say, flat out better than the old system at first glance!<br /> <br /> Some things I'm waiting for, but if I get it right weren't the subject of this playtest:<br /> <br /> - merits/flaws and specializations, I hope they change it to something like NWoD/SR, since that could open up space for more interesting stuff, like fighting styles and such<br /> - how more complex tasks will work<br /> - how they sync the different lines' unique stats (like conscience, etc.)? They want more crossover (which I'm happy about), so I hope they're thinking about it from the beginning.<br /> - how important and pervasive the narrative mechanics will be<br /> <br /> Also, could any of you write a little more about the combat mechanics? How different is it from the old system?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-15-2017, 04:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T14:13:11-07:00","id":1092952,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Herbert_West</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092798#post1092798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Could we get a cliffnotes version, please?</div> </div> </div> </div>I forget to share this. These were the points I took away, which I made notes of:<br /> <br /> Engagement is greater than &quot;fun&quot;<br /> The value of games is demonstrable and observable<br /> Games address human needs - they are for everyone<br /> Engage others with/in games and you will enjoy them more yourself<br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T14:33:45-07:00","id":1092958,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092952#post1092952\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I forget to share this. These were the points I took away, which I made notes of:<br /> <br /> Engagement is greater than &quot;fun&quot;<br /> The value of games is demonstrable and observable<br /> Games address human needs - they are for everyone<br /> Engage others with/in games and you will enjoy them more yourself<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not to be a snarky asshole, but those are, I think, quite evident things. Not that it hurts to actually state them from time to time. I still see game reviewers struggling to frame enjoyment in terms other than fun.<br /> <br /> No offense intended.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5238-herbert_west","name":"Herbert_West","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5238_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"473"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T15:31:34-07:00","id":1092986,"title":"","content":"You should maybe reflect more on these ideas and read deeper. Simple ideas often conceal much deeper truths which are then glossed over. For example, in point two, several experiments have been done which yield results that would surprise most people.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T20:45:28-07:00","id":1093087,"title":"","content":"Something just occurred to me: in the V5 presentation at the Grand Masquerade last year they showed the V5 with the traditional red rose cover. In this keynote, where they showed the concepts of the first three books (system, Camarilla, Anarchs) the first had the picture with the vampire girl from the mobile app game. I hope It won't be the case, I was really glad to presumably getting back the red rose on the core book and it's definitely a lot better visually than that picture, aside from being traditional for VtM.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-15T22:11:23-07:00","id":1093106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093087#post1093087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I hope It won't be the case, I was really glad to presumably getting back the red rose on the core book and it's definitely a lot better visually than that picture, aside from being traditional for VtM.</div> </div> </div> </div>Contact Mary Lee and let her know, she is the new art director and she was asking for views from the community just like this. She wants to know all about what we think the looks for clans should be like too. Dont forget to say why. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T05:51:47-07:00","id":1093192,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092817#post1092817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2157_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2157\" data-vbnamecard=\"2157\">deejay</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2507_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2507\" data-vbnamecard=\"2507\">Caitiff Primogen</a> . Thank you. I've gone one question if you don't mind: if there was a list of compulsions,could you tell me what were the ones for the nosferatu clan?</div> </div> </div> </div>The playtest only had Ventrue and Toreador pregens, so I don't think any rules for Nos were included. At least I don't remember seeing any.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T06:00:21-07:00","id":1093199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CaptOtter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092910#post1092910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For some reason I feel like this approach is fraught with the potential for gonzo aburdity. How does it occur to anyone that the ego-driven, interpersonal histrionics of individual LARPers is equal to having talented, professional writers writing a compelling story and materials.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're overestimating the frequency and impact of games like these. I've not gotten any indication that they're going to replace their writing staff with event LARPs. We're not even sure how much influence Enlightenment In Blood will actually have on the written metaplot.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T09:08:03-07:00","id":1093290,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093192#post1093192\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The playtest only had Ventrue and Toreador pregens, so I don't think any rules for Nos were included. At least I don't remember seeing any.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Someone elsewhere asked about combat rolls. Did it seem to be one-roll combat rolls? Or did you still attack/dodge/damage/soak?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T11:48:15-07:00","id":1093361,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093290#post1093290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Someone elsewhere asked about combat rolls. Did it seem to be one-roll combat rolls? Or did you still attack/dodge/damage/soak?</div> </div> </div> </div>Combat was covered during the rules briefing and was in the packets we had, but I don't remember it very well and the group I ran for actually managed to avoid combat completely so it never came up at the table.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:07:48-07:00","id":1093392,"title":"","content":"It was one roll, and combatants damaged each other. Armour helped to reduce damage, No soak, no dodge, no damage roll. Damage was based on attack roll and weapon used. It was made clear that we were to expect much more development, but that this simplicity would remain a key focus. One roll whenever possible is a key design goal. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:24:43-07:00","id":1093397,"title":"","content":"My friends character sheet<br /> \u200b<br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpcDNtME9TU0dwQXM\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpcDNtME9TU0dwQXM\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpcDNtME9TU0dwQXM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpcDNtME9TU0dwQXM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> You will see they were using the Virtue/Vice system from CoD but Karim said that may change later and was perhaps just for that day.<br /> <br /> I would also like to share this, which is the result of the clan poll they commissioned:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpQmp0bktrc2lQMWc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpQmp0bktrc2lQMWc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpQmp0bktrc2lQMWc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpQmp0bktrc2lQMWc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:39:58-07:00","id":1093404,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2157_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2157\" data-vbnamecard=\"2157\">deejay</a> <br /> Thank you. Interesting that the sheet doesn't have a specialization for each attribute. Wonder if they just forgot that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T13:48:20-07:00","id":1093408,"title":"","content":"They were experimenting and so the specialisations were very sparse but varied. They said 4 or more dots for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T15:54:04-07:00","id":1093432,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093106#post1093106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Contact Mary Lee and let her know, she is the new art director and she was asking for views from the community just like this. She wants to know all about what we think the looks for clans should be like too. Dont forget to say why.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks, I'll do! Could you tell me what channels she want us to use for that? Does she have a public email address, or should I wrote to her on fb/twitter?<br /> <br /> I wrote some letters to the info-white-wolf address, but I don't really know how to communicate more directly with any of them. It just seems wrong to wrote fb messages...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093392#post1093392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was one roll, and combatants damaged each other. Armour helped to reduce damage, No soak, no dodge, no damage roll. Damage was based on attack roll and weapon used. It was made clear that we were to expect much more development, but that this simplicity would remain a key focus. One roll whenever possible is a key design goal.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I hope it'll develop much farther that! Ok, Martin said it repeatedly that it isn't primarily a combat.focused power fantasy, but a social one (although I think that's a very specific and somewhat narrowed to VtM opinion), but I think the game still needs a robust combat system, since violence is pretty much a staple of the games in many cases, to some extent. I'm not against streamlining, but I want active defense mechanics, a reasonable level of simulation, a sensible initiative system and a workable multiple actions one. They don't have to have 10+ maneuvers and tables of weapons in the core book, content like that could be perfectly fine in a latter supplement, but the game needs a not totally oversimplified combat system, IMO.<br /> <br /> Wait and see, wait and see, oh that's just killin' me! <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You will see they were using the Virtue/Vice system from CoD but Karim said that may change later and was perhaps just for that day. </div> </div> </div>Really, <i>really </i>hope so! Never really liked the virtue/vice thing, I think it was among the missteps of NWoD. I always thought nature and demeanor are much more evocative and clear and also more flexible.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I would also like to share this, which is the result of the clan poll they commissioned: </div> </div> </div>I was seriously surprised by that chart. I thought the Malkavians would be among the well-liked, but first???? And Tremere (that utterly baffled me) and Gangrel are being the next ones by a long shot???? Honestly I'd have expected Toreador, Ventrue, Brujah, or Lasombra among the first 3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-16-2017, 07:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-16T19:40:55-07:00","id":1093503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093432#post1093432\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Really, really hope so! Never really liked the virtue/vice thing, I think it was among the missteps of NWoD. I always thought nature and demeanor are much more evocative and clear and also more flexible.</div> </div> </div> </div>In a conversation with Karim he mentioned that while he likes aspects of Requiem and would like to crib certain ideas from it he explicitly doesn't want to just &quot;make it like Requiem.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was seriously surprised by that chart. I thought the Malkavians would be among the well-liked, but first???? And Tremere (that utterly baffled me) and Gangrel are being the next ones by a long shot???? Honestly I'd have expected Toreador, Ventrue, Brujah, or Lasombra among the first 3. </div> </div> </div>Gangrel and Tremere have always been popular and populous clans in most of the groups I've played with. Malkavians surprised me though (and I say this as an avid Malkavian player).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T00:22:26-07:00","id":1093561,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093503#post1093503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In a conversation with Karim he mentioned that while he likes aspects of Requiem and would like to crib certain ideas from it he explicitly doesn't want to just &quot;make it like Requiem.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not necessarily a bad thing (I liked some of the ideas in Requiem) and my problem isn't that &quot;it was like that in Requiem&quot; (or, in this case, in NWoD in general), but that, in my opinion, the virtue/vice system is flat out inferior to the nature/demeanor one and everyone I know liked the later better. I think it's good the CofD 2nds wen back in that direction.<br /> <br /> Also, borrowing some ideas from Requiem could be good, I'm not against it, but I think they should be very careful with that. The setting, what we know about it this far already goes into Requiem's direction quite a lot. People like WoD for being WoD, making Masquerade too much like Requiem would be counterproductive, IMO and also wouldn't be fair toward Requiem. I'd also consider the problem of why change something like that, after 4 editions of working well? It's not like the combat mechanics, or the feeding one, it's character personality description, with minor influence on mechanics and it worked. i just think it's unnecessary to mess with.<br /> <br /> So anyway, I hope the guys will find a good balance there, I just also hope they'll go back to nature/demeanor or something similar.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Gangrel and Tremere have always been popular and populous clans in most of the groups I've played with. Malkavians surprised me though (and I say this as an avid Malkavian player). </div> </div> </div>Hmmm, interesting. Normal Gangrel, or city Gangrel?<br /> <br /> My perspective is skewed by the Budapest scene, where players generally have an overwhelming favor for Brujah (there's an ongoing joke in the LARP scene tht Budapest is really Brujahpest...) with Torreador, Ventrue, Lasombra and Malkav also being popular. I suspect Malkavians has a worldwide influx because of things like Suicide Squad/Harley Quinn and Jeanette in Bloodlines. I just always thought of them as one of the most popular clans, but never the most.<br /> <br /> Tremere... it's just not popular here, there are few people in general, who likes to play the pyramid and with that much restriction. I get that vampire sorcerers are cool and that they are mechanically strong, but I never really felt that much inclination to play one, because of the fluff reasons and I think that's the majority's opinion over there.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 05-17-2017, 03:26 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T00:39:17-07:00","id":1093567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092742#post1092742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still at the airport in Germany but I figure I'll add my own two cents to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2157_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2157\" data-vbnamecard=\"2157\">deejay</a> has posted. I'm not going to get too hung up on system minutiae as that's the most likely thing to change going forward. Instead I'll focusing more on mechanical concepts and applications.<br /> <br /> ...</div> </div> </div> </div>Awesomely informative post.<br /> <br /> Did Humanity come up at all? How was it handled?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://blood-and-bourbon.obsidianportal.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Blood and Bourbon</a>, my New Orleans-based Vampire chronicle.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3110-false-epiphany","name":"False Epiphany","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3110_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"748"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T00:50:29-07:00","id":1093570,"title":"","content":"Humanity didn't really come up, it's for a future playtest cycle. (I also got in as a player - and the character I got had a typo where his Humanity was initially 0 rather than 6...)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T01:19:20-07:00","id":1093577,"title":"","content":"The talented and helpful Father Sebastian has put up the WoD keynote speech for everyone -<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z9qpAosKdgI\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z9qpAosKdgI\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z9qpAosKdgI\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z9qpAosKdgI </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> @PMark - Dont be shy! Facebook is cool. The gang are very approachable and keen to hear from us. I have Dhaunae De Virs email, but not Marys. I am sure Dhaunae can put you in touch with the art director though.<br /> <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#52363a33273c33377c3637243b2012253a3b26377f253d3e347c313d3f\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"aecac6cfdbc0cfcb80cacbd8c7dceed9c6c7dacb83d9c1c2c880cdc1c3\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2157,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","user":"deejay","date":". 05-17-2017, 04:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay","name":"deejay","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2157_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T13:51:29-07:00","id":1093788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093577#post1093577\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> @PMark - Dont be shy! Facebook is cool. The gang are very approachable and keen to hear from us. I have Dhaunae De Virs email, but not Marys. I am sure Dhaunae can put you in touch with the art director though.<br /> <a href=\"/cdn-cgi/l/email-protection#c5a1ada4b0aba4a0eba1a0b3acb785b2adacb1a0e8b2aaa9a3eba6aaa8\"><span class=\"__cf_email__\" data-cfemail=\"22464a43574c43470c4647544b5062554a4b56470f554d4e440c414d4f\">[email&#160;protected]</span></a></div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks for the answer! Honestly, I wrote a few emails to their general info mail address (which Dhaunae answered to) a few months earlier, but I didn't contacted any of them through personal channels. Don't know, I just feel writing directly to someone who aren't my personal acquaintance on FB like that a bit...intrusive? Anyway, I'd take a chance with any of the possible channels you mentioned! It'd be really good to talk to them directly, since I can't really go to these big events, sadly.<br /> <br /> Also, I hope they'd kick in a full-blown open playtest interface, like WotC, that would be amazing!<br /> <br /> Thanks again!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T14:49:02-07:00","id":1093831,"title":"","content":"They mentioned plans for a more open playtest in the near future...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Craig Oxbrow<br /> <b>The Trinity Continuum</b> freelancer","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/221-craig-oxbrow","name":"Craig Oxbrow","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar221_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"608"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:07:42-07:00","id":1093846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Craig Oxbrow</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093831#post1093831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They mentioned plans for a more open playtest in the near future...</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably at gen con or grand masquerade.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T15:20:22-07:00","id":1093857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>deejay</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093397#post1093397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would also like to share this, which is the result of the clan poll they commissioned:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"b-bbcode b-bbcode__url b-bbcode__url--preview\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpQmp0bktrc2lQMWc\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"urlimg_container\"> <img class=\"js-img-fallback\" src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/default/google-material/image_placeholder.svg\"> </a> <div class=\"urlinfo\"> <div class=\"title ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpQmp0bktrc2lQMWc\" target=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpQmp0bktrc2lQMWc\" target=\"_blank\"> https://drive.google.com/open?id=0B2K7ygx29YDpQmp0bktrc2lQMWc </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div></div> </div> </div> </div>That spread looks fairly intuitive until you get to the #1 poll choice, which was a serious record scratch moment for me.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T17:34:30-07:00","id":1093913,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Matt the Bruins fan</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1093857#post1093857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That spread looks fairly intuitive until you get to the #1 poll choice, which was a serious record scratch moment for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>I felt the same way for a minute, until I realized that the OP forums make up only a very small portion of the fanbase. Facebook, Twitter, etc. are all huge fans of Malkavians.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-17T23:32:59-07:00","id":1094006,"title":"","content":"I'm also curious how that breaks down between different media fans. The survey wasn't just TT players, or just LARP players.<br /> <br /> If a lot of people are, for example, coming from the VtMB computer game crowd, I can see it significantly upping the Malkavian and Tremere responses (Malkavians, Tremere, and Nosferatu are the only Clans in the game where there's some significant changes in what happens, and the Nosferatu option is basically the hard option, while Malks are the funniest and Tremere are really powerful).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T13:07:22-07:00","id":1094276,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1094006#post1094006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm also curious how that breaks down between different media fans. The survey wasn't just TT players, or just LARP players.<br /> <br /> If a lot of people are, for example, coming from the VtMB computer game crowd, I can see it significantly upping the Malkavian and Tremere responses (Malkavians, Tremere, and Nosferatu are the only Clans in the game where there's some significant changes in what happens, and the Nosferatu option is basically the hard option, while Malks are the funniest and Tremere are really powerful).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, that could be a thing. Also, there are tons of people not filling out the survey, for example I don't think a lot of gamers from Hungary bothered with it. So, for a lot of reasons, it could be quite skewed, but still it is very interesting and surprising to me!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T14:34:25-07:00","id":1094308,"title":"","content":"There is also the concerning trend that playing Malkavian is seen as a true test. People who think they are sophisticated role players chose them to show how brilliant they are... only to hog the spotlight. At least that is what friends of mine and to a certain extend i myself have observed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T18:18:32-07:00","id":1094372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1094308#post1094308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the concerning trend that playing Malkavian is seen as a true test. People who think they are sophisticated role players chose them to show how brilliant they are... only to hog the spotlight. At least that is what friends of mine and to a certain extend i myself have observed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sort of like who can handle playing the Joker. Mark Hamill? Yes. Jared Leto? Ha ha ha ha ha no.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-18T23:00:05-07:00","id":1094436,"title":"","content":"Strange. My friends playing VtM preffer other clans. Ventrue, Tzimisce, Lasombra. Tremere. The big 4.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1784-werewolf43","name":"werewolf43","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1784_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"315"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T05:04:31-07:00","id":1098730,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1092742#post1092742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm still at the airport in Germany but I figure I'll add my own two cents to what <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2157-deejay\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar2157_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"2157\" data-vbnamecard=\"2157\">deejay</a> has posted. I'm not going to get too hung up on system minutiae as that's the most likely thing to change going forward. Instead I'll focusing more on mechanical concepts and applications.<br /> <br /> The &quot;big thing&quot; that it seemed like this was a testbed for is the Hunger system as a replacement for Blood Points. The basic idea is that rather than decreasing the amount of blood you have you increase the amount of hunger you have. Rather than spending Blood Points you instead &quot;Rouse the Blood&quot; to accomplish a variety of things (basically all the same things you spend blood for under the current rules). A few subtle but important inclusions are that you must Rouse the Blood to awaken each night, any vampire must Rouse in order to not appear dead, and all uses of Disciplines require Rousing. You keep track of how many times you Rouse the Blood in a scene and at the end of that scene you roll that many dice. Any dice that don't roll a success add to your Hunger (a scale of 1-5). Any time you make a skill roll or skill-based Discipline roll you have a number of dice in your pool replaced by &quot;Hunger dice,&quot; equal to your Hunger rating. These dice function like normal dice and can contribute successes, but if any of them roll a 1 you gain a temporary Compulsion from your Beast (note that 1s do not subtract from successes in these rules so you aren't getting double-whammied or anything). Compulsions are tics of your predatory vampiric nature that can vary in severity depending on the number of Hunger dice that rolled a 1. In the game I ran a Toreador was overwhelmed with strong emotion for someone in the scene, a Ventrue felt compelled to assert his dominance and leadership over the group, and another Ventrue felt incredible anxiety at the lack of order and structure they had without guidance from their superiors. These were all pretty minor Compulsions and we didn't have anyone fail badly enough to pull one of the nastier ones (though one character was walking around with 4 Hunger for a bit).<br /> Hunger is reduced by feeding, shock of all shocks. There was a scale that told you how much Hunger was removed by feeding on what. IIRC animals removed 2 and feeding on a human without killing them removed 3. Feeding on a human and killing them in the process removes 4 and is also the only way to reduce your Hunger below 1 (temporarily), otherwise all vampires are assumed to always have at least 1 Hunger.<br /> Honestly, it worked pretty well and everyone I talked to seemed to feel likewise. It needs refinement, something even Karim said in a couple conversations I had with him, but the core concept and system is actually surprisingly thematic and functional.<br /> <br /> In this set of rules the extent of &quot;you are what you eat&quot; was getting small, temporary bonuses from feeding on certain people. They said this is something they want to continue with but are still developing a proper system for. At this point though assuming the final system for that has broadly similar outcomes to the listed effects in the playtest it <i>doesn't</i> seem like that addition to the system is going to be as huge and game-changing as some people were thinking.<br /> <br /> The other addition that was generally a hit (with exceptions I'll talk about) was &quot;Success With Consequences,&quot; wherein if the number of successes you rolled fell exactly one short of the number you needed you could choose to succeed but have the ST add in some complication or consequence. It only happened a couple times at my table and worked well both times. Other people I talked to reported similarly with the exception of one table where it apparently happened so often it became cumbersome to the flow. Seems like something that depends a great deal on the fall of the dice and the kinds of things the ST decides to throw in.<br /> <br /> There are other smaller things I could go into, but deejay already mostly touched on them and I feel they're fairly minor details to really heavily scrutinize at this early stage.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interesting system. Still feels a bit like Vampire: the Something Else instead of Vampire: the Masquerade in it's tone, but at least that's a plausible and potentially fun system. Especially with the &quot;yawye&quot;-system toned down (hopefully to a level that can be ignored). Just wish they wouldn't change old core rules just for the sake of it, rather polish and tweak what there is.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with a blood pool removed and replaced by a hunger pool, how does generations scale? Or is that removed entirely now? Do you know?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T14:13:51-07:00","id":1098891,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crytash</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1094308#post1094308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There is also the concerning trend that playing Malkavian is seen as a true test. People who think they are sophisticated role players chose them to show how brilliant they are... only to hog the spotlight. At least that is what friends of mine and to a certain extend i myself have observed.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's interesting that that's a &quot;true test&quot;--and now that you mention it, I can see it. However, I've always found the real test of a good or brilliant player has been how they play a centuries-old vampire--someone who has been a vampire ten or fifteen or even twenty times longer than they were human. And while there's almost certainly no one correct way to do it, neither would I say there is any one correct way to play a Malkavian (what with madness and the curse being portrayed as such a unique and personal thing to any so afflicted). But just like the obvious trap in playing a Malkavian is to fall into the &quot;Fish Malk&quot; trap, I see the trap of playing a very old vampire as being the nigh universal adoption of a haughty, patrician demeanor.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Sig","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2319-captotter","name":"CaptOtter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2319_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"405"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-31T19:06:13-07:00","id":1098974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>IgnyteZero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1098730#post1098730\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Interesting system. Still feels a bit like Vampire: the Something Else instead of Vampire: the Masquerade in it's tone, but at least that's a plausible and potentially fun system. Especially with the &quot;yawye&quot;-system toned down (hopefully to a level that can be ignored). Just wish they wouldn't change old core rules just for the sake of it, rather polish and tweak what there is.<br /> <br /> Anyway, with a blood pool removed and replaced by a hunger pool, how does generations scale? Or is that removed entirely now? Do you know?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They've said Generation exists, but it's harder to determine the true Generation of someone, but we have no mechanics or anything that came up during the playtest, from what was posted by people who played in the paytest. And honestly, innovate or die. Even D&amp;D has innovated and changed things, while keeping a 'core' mechanic (in this instance, scads of d10s). Introducing narrative mechanics and other things are an attempt to modernize the design. I mean, if D&amp;D never changed anything, we'd still have THAC0.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T02:58:47-07:00","id":1099087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1098974#post1098974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> They've said Generation exists, but it's harder to determine the true Generation of someone, but we have no mechanics or anything that came up during the playtest, from what was posted by people who played in the paytest. And honestly, innovate or die. Even D&amp;D has innovated and changed things, while keeping a 'core' mechanic (in this instance, scads of d10s). Introducing narrative mechanics and other things are an attempt to modernize the design. I mean, if D&amp;D never changed anything, we'd still have THAC0.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue that THAC0 isn't a mechanic as closely knit to the spirit and point of D&amp;D as blood pools have been to V:tm.<br /> <br /> I'd also argue to not fix that which is not broken. Don't change things for changes sake, just to leave your own dent on history. THAC0 was always weird. Blood pools haven't been.<br /> <br /> I'd even argue that rpg's decline never were because of weird rules and lack of narrative mechanics. Not the least. It was because of social stigma and the sudden low threshold of modern computer/video games.<br /> <br /> But, other than that, maybe you're right. I'm still openly skeptic about it, but I'm not against it. Might be the best Vampire-game ever made in the end. Who knows?<br /> <br /> Harder to determine someones generation is something I'm all for though.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T10:01:31-07:00","id":1099199,"title":"","content":"Here's kind of the funny thing about blood pool vs hunger. Their actual mechanical outcomes are about ninety percent similar, the differences are largely aesthetic (which is not the same thing as cosmetic). In a very real way its the difference between a glass half-full or half-empty. With blood points the frame of reference is how full are you, with hunger its how empty are you. What's the difference? Why make that change? Some people aren't going to see that as a big enough deal to warrant mucking about with a core system, even aesthetically. Personally though I get what they're going for and I think it actually does manage to capture the essence of what Vampire is better than the system it has to this point used, at least in concept. <br /> <br /> Interestingly the same thing actually applies in D&amp;D. I recently ran a 1st edition AD&amp;D game for the first time in forever and for a group of people with zero previous exposure to it. As part of this I had to refamiliarize myself with Attack Matrices and find a way to present them to the players in a way that was accessible and easy to interface with. In the process of doing this I eventually realized that the progression from Attack Matrix to THAC0 to BAB wasn't a line but a tight orbit around a central nucleus. The exact same interaction was happening in the die rolls but the frame of reference for that interaction had evolved into something more reflective of the intent and which renders that intent legible to the players. <br /> <br /> Back on V5. They said that Generation still exists, but they're still working on how exactly that's going to interact with Hunger. As mentioned earlier they're also trying to move away from Generation as an objective quantity to make the deep history of vampirism more mysterious. Since that's something I've already been doing in my games for a while now I'm a fan of this direction.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T20:00:16-07:00","id":1099373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1099199#post1099199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's kind of the funny thing about blood pool vs hunger. Their actual mechanical outcomes are about ninety percent similar, the differences are largely aesthetic (which is not the same thing as cosmetic). In a very real way its the difference between a glass half-full or half-empty. With blood points the frame of reference is how full are you, with hunger its how empty are you. What's the difference? Why make that change? Some people aren't going to see that as a big enough deal to warrant mucking about with a core system, even aesthetically. Personally though I get what they're going for and I think it actually does manage to capture the essence of what Vampire is better than the system it has to this point used, at least in concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>I thought along those lines too. They aren't that dissimilar. The old rules handled hunger as well and the new ones have a &quot;fuels track&quot; in composure too. Mybe they just want to avoid the whole notion of blood points, of players thinking of blood as a resource management thing. Also, I think it shifts the focus a bit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Back on V5. They said that Generation still exists, but they're still working on how exactly that's going to interact with Hunger. As mentioned earlier they're also trying to move away from Generation as an objective quantity to make the deep history of vampirism more mysterious. Since that's something I've already been doing in my games for a while now I'm a fan of this direction. </div> </div> </div>Hmmm. Generation is a big one in VtM (and rightly so, it adds to the setting) and I don't want it to be a strictly fluff-thing, but I always wanted it to not be as a hard cap on power as it was, so it might turn out to be a good thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 06-02-2017, 03:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T12:59:30-07:00","id":1099616,"title":"","content":"The difference in Hunger vs Blood Pool is two-fold. First, Hunger describes on what your character is experiencing while Blood Pool is a fuel abstraction. They refer to the same thing (you need blood to keep going) but there is a change in focus. Second, the Hunger mechanic is less exact. With blood pools, you know exactly how much juice you have left. With Hunger, you don't. You take risks and hope the dice favor you. This helps build tension. Resource management generally doesn't.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T15:10:57-07:00","id":1099658,"title":"","content":"I'm not sure I really buy that (though of course we haven't seen the final version and most people haven't gotten to play it).<br /> <br /> &quot;I have 2 Hunger dice,&quot; and, &quot;I have 7 out of 10 blood points,&quot; are pretty much equal to me in terms of what they tell me about what my character is experiencing. I haven't seen any of the stuff the emerges from the rouse/hunger/feed cycle in the large Hunger system that you can't do with a &quot;fuel abstraction&quot; system. Beast in the CofD demonstrates that just fine.<br /> <br /> I also think the &quot;exactness&quot; thing is a bit off. Hunger doesn't make &quot;how much juice you have,&quot; opaque via randomness, it just tosses tracking juice out the window. From the (again admittedly very early) previews, the Hunger system lets you rouse infinitely if you're willing to deal with the consequences. A vampire never technically has to drink blood with the Hunger system as previewed (unless frenzies in the new system force that but I haven't seen anyone say this about it). It isn't less exact, it just doesn't track juice at all. Which isn't a bad thing in my mind, I just don't think it's a fair comparison.<br /> <br /> The &quot;builds up tension&quot; part is also very subjective. Having a core source of dramatic tension be at the whim of the dice all the time gets old. This is probably coming from almost two decades of playing Mage, but after long enough random dice of badness (like Paradox) just become a resource you're managing. Managing a static resource or a variable resource largely grows into the same thing over time. It reminds me a lot of how Paradox in Mage 2e played out: people that were new to the system generally got excited at first, but after seeing their character blow up because of a bad dice roll too many times, it lost its edge, and they noticed more experienced players easily evading Paradox completely because they'd learned exactly where the sweet spot of how much Paradox you can built up without a worst-case-scenario roll actually meaning much.<br /> <br /> As well, any fun of reducing resource management is blunted by the book keeping of three things to track (number of Rouses, number of Hunger dice, Composure pool), adding a new fuel abstraction style trait (Composure), and having to check for Hunger dice pushing your character to do things every roll (save when you kill people for Hunger 0)..","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 06-02-2017, 06:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T18:36:09-07:00","id":1099706,"title":"","content":"As a casual interjection, the creative director also noted that he planned on using a similar &quot;rousing&quot; system for other games' resources. I have serious doubts that this will work well for Werewolf, because it tracks and determines things in a fashion exactly opposite from Vampire in terms of self-control and frenzies, and Gnosis is neither here nor there with regard to how you regain it and any psychological effects thereof. Unless he wants everyone going into Rapture like Ratkin, which would be a tremendous change to, well, everything in Werewolf.<br /> <br /> (Thought exercise ahead)<br /> <br /> So, if, say, Rage, worked anything like this, it would end up looking more like Rage replacing Composure and &quot;rousing&quot; being some kind of fatigue, and you'd be trying to ride a line in spending Rage to avoid getting too calm or tired; frenzies and anything that angered you would actually allow you to wipe away some fatigue. Hopefully, you wouldn't be outright Losing the Wolf all of the time you got really tired, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-02T21:55:41-07:00","id":1099753,"title":"","content":"I think thought exercises of trying to extrapolate on Werewolf are problematic simply because it's so dependent on how big of a change the rest things get.<br /> <br /> The Rousing system bolted onto vampire fairly easily, because vampires didn't have to juggle two different juice types. While it simplified every Discipline activation cost to one Rousing (though in theory there's nothing that stops more potent powers from costing more), and many other vampire innate abilities cost blood anyway, that's not really a big deal.<br /> <br /> Since werewolf divides things up between Gnosis and Rage, you can't do something like that. Having stepping sideways or activating Talens/Fetishes &quot;Rouse Rage&quot; doesn't make any sense. So either the whole thing needs to be reworked (like Forsaken did by moving all werewolf powers to Essence and having Rage be a state characters enter), or the Hunger/Rouse model isn't going to be a good fit.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T04:07:39-07:00","id":1099789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1099199#post1099199\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Here's kind of the funny thing about blood pool vs hunger. Their actual mechanical outcomes are about ninety percent similar, the differences are largely aesthetic (which is not the same thing as cosmetic). In a very real way its the difference between a glass half-full or half-empty. With blood points the frame of reference is how full are you, with hunger its how empty are you. What's the difference? Why make that change? Some people aren't going to see that as a big enough deal to warrant mucking about with a core system, even aesthetically. Personally though I get what they're going for and I think it actually does manage to capture the essence of what Vampire is better than the system it has to this point used, at least in concept.<br /> <br /> Interestingly the same thing actually applies in D&amp;D. I recently ran a 1st edition AD&amp;D game for the first time in forever and for a group of people with zero previous exposure to it. As part of this I had to refamiliarize myself with Attack Matrices and find a way to present them to the players in a way that was accessible and easy to interface with. In the process of doing this I eventually realized that the progression from Attack Matrix to THAC0 to BAB wasn't a line but a tight orbit around a central nucleus. The exact same interaction was happening in the die rolls but the frame of reference for that interaction had evolved into something more reflective of the intent and which renders that intent legible to the players.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> When World of Warcraft vanilla was in beta the creators designed an experience system lowered the amount of experience you got because they wanted to be proactive. They wanted you to play a couple of hours and not binge play WoW. The reduction was from 100% gradually down to 50%.<br /> People despised it. It was a major turn of for everyone involved and was seen as a major no-no. Blizzard thought about this and &quot;changed the system. The players LOVED the new system called &quot;resting&quot;. <br /> What Blizzard actually did was simple. They doubled the experience needed to get a level, but they also gave you the state of resting after you did not play the game for an amount of time. A certain amount of exp would be counted double.<br /> <br /> It is quintessentially the same mechanic, with a similar mechanical outcome, but the reactions and emotions of the players were completely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T13:03:29-07:00","id":1100196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1099658#post1099658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;I have 2 Hunger dice,&quot; and, &quot;I have 7 out of 10 blood points,&quot; are pretty much equal to me in terms of what they tell me about what my character is experiencing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Similar, but not equal. For one thing, one is explicit about what your character is experiencing: Hunger. On a scale of 1-5, this is how hungry you are. The other is more abstract, which means it can provide the same information (&quot;I have 70% of my blood pool so, on a scale of 1-10, my hunger is a 3.&quot;) but that remove is important. You have to work harder to get the same information and it is easier to ignore. The second part is that with the blood pool, you know you have X invokes of Y power before you can't use it anymore. With hunger, you know that the more you use your powers, the higher your risk of losing control, but there is no certainty. It is a dice roll, so you just have a probability. That makes a big difference. The risk is something evocative, something you feel when you roll the dice, and it parallels what your character is feeling when they push themselves. Deciding whether or not to spend blood points now or save until later is a cold calculation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I also think the &quot;exactness&quot; thing is a bit off. Hunger doesn't make &quot;how much juice you have,&quot; opaque via randomness, it just tosses tracking juice out the window. From the (again admittedly very early) previews, the Hunger system lets you rouse infinitely if you're willing to deal with the consequences. A vampire never technically has to drink blood with the Hunger system as previewed (unless frenzies in the new system force that but I haven't seen anyone say this about it). It isn't less exact, it just doesn't track juice at all. Which isn't a bad thing in my mind, I just don't think it's a fair comparison. </div> </div> </div>I don't follow your logic at all. You pretty much concede to my point but then claim they aren't the same thing. Except that your whole argument is based on them being the same thing. So... I don't know how to respond?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The &quot;builds up tension&quot; part is also very subjective. Having a core source of dramatic tension be at the whim of the dice all the time gets old. This is probably coming from almost two decades of playing Mage, but after long enough random dice of badness (like Paradox) just become a resource you're managing. Managing a static resource or a variable resource largely grows into the same thing over time. It reminds me a lot of how Paradox in Mage 2e played out: people that were new to the system generally got excited at first, but after seeing their character blow up because of a bad dice roll too many times, it lost its edge, and they noticed more experienced players easily evading Paradox completely because they'd learned exactly where the sweet spot of how much Paradox you can built up without a worst-case-scenario roll actually meaning much. </div> </div> </div>I feel like the issues you have with Paradox do not apply here. As you note, this isn't simply a &quot;roll or explode&quot; system, this has a couple layers and includes the risk of giving into your clan weakness, which I think is really neat. It puts that interesting aspect of the setting in a more prominent place.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As well, any fun of reducing resource management is blunted by the book keeping of three things to track (number of Rouses, number of Hunger dice, Composure pool), adding a new fuel abstraction style trait (Composure), and having to check for Hunger dice pushing your character to do things every roll (save when you kill people for Hunger 0).. </div> </div> </div>I don't see Composure as a fuel trait because it isn't just something you spend, it is also something you roll. This makes it much more interesting, since spending Composure doesn't just mean you don't have that point to spend later, it means you have a smaller die pool to roll for some period of time. It is more uncertain than resource management because if you never have to make a roll on that pool, then you are fine. If you are in a situation where you have to roll against it many times, that little bit of control you kept is now /really/ expensive. The tricky part is trying to gauge which position you are in. And, again, it is not just managing an abstract number, Composure describes exactly what it is and, again, the experience of your character. If my composure is down to 1 out of 5, I know what my character is feeling. They are barely holding it together. <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T14:30:32-07:00","id":1100218,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1100196#post1100196\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Similar, but not equal.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not arguing against this. I'm arguing that (1) they're not so different as to have a major change on the feel of the game, and (2) that having played a game with a random/variable consequence pool to track, over time a lot of the things being cited as making the Hunger mechanics so interesting do not withstand long term play with the system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> On a scale of 1-5, this is how hungry you are. </div> </div> </div>Or 0-10 how full you are.<br /> <br /> A 1-5 rating of hunger isn't explicit because &quot;hunger&quot; isn't something we experience on a distinct scale. You can't tell me in any explicit way what a &quot;Hunger 4&quot; feeling is than you can say what a, &quot;Fullness 5&quot; feeling is.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You have to work harder to get the same information and it is easier to ignore. </div> </div> </div>It's hard to ignore Hunger because the game forces you to roll Hunger dice all the time, not because tracking hunger is more explicitly informative than tracking fullness. If you did something like take the Satiety Conditions from BtP and attached them to the default blood-pool in VtM, people would never ignore their blood-pools because there would be important mechanical effects besides how much juice they've got. And it is even more informative to what a character is feeling because the Satiety Conditions can convey what a character is actively feeling far better that an abstract scale of a subjective emotional experience that only informs you mechanically of what it means via randomized results.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The second part is that with the blood pool, you know you have X invokes of Y power before you can't use it anymore. With hunger, you know that the more you use your powers, the higher your risk of losing control, but there is no certainty. </div> </div> </div>And my problem is that with long enough experience with the game, players will invariably set a X invokes of Y powers value before they'll stop using them. It just becomes emergent from the math of the rest of the system rather than explicitly stated. This also ends up having a negative impact on cooperative play between players and the ST because it shifts the burden on the ST to constantly present situations that are designed to push players to exceed their self-imposed X value, which creates antagonism instead of fun.<br /> <br /> If the players aren't going to go past whatever the emergent X value is on their own, then what's the point? There needs to be some sort of reward for engaging with it, but at the moment Rousing too much is all downsides. IME this just results in players feeling &quot;taxed&quot; for doing awesome things or worse things just to make the scene happen, especially with how everything vampiric is a Rouse and Hunger dice are omnipresent in the play test descriptions. Again, I go back to the Satiety Conditions as a counter example. How sated your Beast is effects game play in a much more play-oriented fashion. Players can pick a Satiety level that generates a Condition that fits their play style/character and get much more meaningful decisions when it comes to invoking things that cost Satiety. The tension of, &quot;do I have my character go out and feed to stock up on invokes because shit's about to get real but lose the bonuses they get for being hungry, or do I risk starving them because I don't have enough invokes even if they're stronger than normal&quot; is a lot more fun to me than, &quot;well if I invoke any more, I'm at the whims of the dice to see if my character flips out and all the consequences there-in.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't follow your logic at all. You pretty much concede to my point but then claim they aren't the same thing. Except that your whole argument is based on them being the same thing. So... I don't know how to respond? </div> </div> </div>I'm saying it's an apples to oranges comparison. I'm not saying that an uncertain resource like Hunger is bad, but since it doesn't directly track juice you can't compare it to blood-points directly in terms of tracking juice.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel like the issues you have with Paradox do not apply here. As you note, this isn't simply a &quot;roll or explode&quot; system, this has a couple layers and includes the risk of giving into your clan weakness, which I think is really neat. It puts that interesting aspect of the setting in a more prominent place. </div> </div> </div>Well, the issues I have with Paradox are something we can go to a final system to look at, and this is a early-alpha preview. We don't know what the final version will look like, so how &quot;roll or explode&quot; it is, is still unknown.<br /> <br /> However, from the play test previews that's where things stand. The more you Rouse (compared to the more you use vulgar magic in Mage) the more you generate Hunger (the more Paradox you get) and the bigger your risk of Frenzy (the bigger the dangers of Backlash). So the parallel seems hard to dispute.<br /> <br /> The insertion of &quot;act more vampire-like&quot; moments from Hunger dice is a neat trick, but it doesn't map well to the Clans as they are now for highlighting the Clan weaknesses. It's fine for things like the Toreador or Brujah where they have immediate and situational emotional weaknesses. It doesn't translate well to a Ventrue's feeding restrictions (which is why I find one of the examples given about what the play group's Ventrue did a bit jarring without the context of that specific character's mentality), or a Nosferatu's physical appearance. So, yes, it's a neat addition, but it doesn't justify any larger issues if they aren't mitigated some other way in the end.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't see Composure as a fuel trait because it isn't just something you spend, it is also something you roll. </div> </div> </div>So... it's like Willpower, Gnosis, Rage, Glamour, etc. etc. I'm not sure that really changes much. It certainly doesn't address the point I was making where the Hunger system as presented as a lot of bookkeeping involved, and this just reinforces the idea that Composure is another resource to manage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It is more uncertain than resource management because if you never have to make a roll on that pool, then you are fine. </div> </div> </div>So... if I'm playing V20 and I'm in a scene where I never have to use a power that requires spending blood, blood points stop being resource management?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If my composure is down to 1 out of 5, I know what my character is feeling. They are barely holding it together. </div> </div> </div>So... what does their temporary Willpower mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T17:31:50-07:00","id":1100274,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1100218#post1100218\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The insertion of &quot;act more vampire-like&quot; moments from Hunger dice is a neat trick, but it doesn't map well to the Clans as they are now for highlighting the Clan weaknesses. It's fine for things like the Toreador or Brujah where they have immediate and situational emotional weaknesses. It doesn't translate well to a Ventrue's feeding restrictions (which is why I find one of the examples given about what the play group's Ventrue did a bit jarring without the context of that specific character's mentality), or a Nosferatu's physical appearance. So, yes, it's a neat addition, but it doesn't justify any larger issues if they aren't mitigated some other way in the end.<br /> <br /> <br /> So... what does their temporary Willpower mean?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just a note, the Compulsions you use Composure on didn't always map to the Clan weaknesses. A Camarilla Ventrue in the playtest listing freaked out about not having any leadership to fall back to when she chose not to spend a Composure on a Compulsion. It causes the vampire to act in an irrational manner, not just their Clan Flaw. To me, it makes sense in terms of what they're wanting to do. Willpower being inner strength and determination, Composure being 'keeping your cool'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1808-elmerg","name":"elmerg","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"539"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T02:42:19-07:00","id":1100381,"title":"","content":"Heavy Arms criticism reflects exactly my own worries after reading the input from the playtests. I don't understand why some seem so eager to defend it as is, it is clearly a very unpolished system right now and that's what playtests are for in the first place; Collect input and criticism.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1099658#post1099658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I also think the &quot;exactness&quot; thing is a bit off. Hunger doesn't make &quot;how much juice you have,&quot; opaque via randomness, it just tosses tracking juice out the window. From the (again admittedly very early) previews, the Hunger system lets you rouse infinitely if you're willing to deal with the consequences. A vampire never technically has to drink blood with the Hunger system as previewed (unless frenzies in the new system force that but I haven't seen anyone say this about it). It isn't less exact, it just doesn't track juice at all. Which isn't a bad thing in my mind, I just don't think it's a fair comparison.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is why I asked about Generation. If Hunger has no bottom, how on earth is generation reflected except trait limits? If a methuselah can expend hunger at the same rate as a fledgling, what's the point? To me it almost seems like it implicates a system without Generations.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-hunters-hunted-ii\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img692/7017/hh2support.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-anarchs-unbound\" target=\"_blank\"> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img703/6636/6kvo.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-mage-the-ascension-20th-anniversary-edition\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img31/2512/25ew.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a> <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/deluxe-w20-book-of-the-wyrm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/507-ignytezero","name":"IgnyteZero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar507_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T03:40:55-07:00","id":1100391,"title":"","content":"The other thing that Generation did mechanically is one of the things I like worst about it as it functioned: resisting mental/social Disciplines (sometimes).<br /> <br /> I could see some design sense to reworking the mind-whammy powers to being resisted with Composure instead of Willpower, and having Generation giving you free Composure to spend solely to resist them, which would then leave the lower Generations with more Composure in general, letting them withstand more of the Rousing/Hunger cycle. But even that would leave Generation as a trait annoyingly too good to pass up compared to ones that are easier to acquire in play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T09:35:21-07:00","id":1100474,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>elmerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1100274#post1100274\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Just a note, the Compulsions you use Composure on didn't always map to the Clan weaknesses. A Camarilla Ventrue in the playtest listing freaked out about not having any leadership to fall back to when she chose not to spend a Composure on a Compulsion. It causes the vampire to act in an irrational manner, not just their Clan Flaw. To me, it makes sense in terms of what they're wanting to do. Willpower being inner strength and determination, Composure being 'keeping your cool'.</div> </div> </div> </div>Technically the &quot;lack of leadership&quot; compulsion was actually one of the Ventrue-specific ones, but you are correct that there were also more general vampiric compulsions. I just focused on the clan-specific ones in the playtest I ran because those were the toys I wanted to play with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T11:39:38-07:00","id":1103868,"title":"","content":"I like the idea behind some of the Hunger mechanics, but I'm not keen on rolling against random charts. I like Blood Whispers and the tie with clan flaws. I'd prefer, though, that they mapped this onto the existing BP system, rather than using a less specific/defined Hunger system that replaces it wholecloth. As Heavy Arms explains, Hunger 0-5 is no easier to imagine than BP 0-10. I also don't like the idea that you run the risk of Hunger as frequently as currently presented. Yes, it can be ever-present, but I'd prefer not to have to constantly swap dice for Hunger dice even for mundane tasks.<br /> <br /> I'd prefer a system where you have Hunger triggers instead, or something narrative-based like Paradox Flaws. Minor triggers have minor effects; more significant ones can cause frenzy or rotschreck. I like the idea of multiple states/impairments somewhere between 'composed' and 'frenzied'. These can be tailored to your character and circumstances, and they might be things you opt to take in order to get a bonus or benefit (e.g., riding the wave). They shouldn't be purely randomised.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer, publisher, performer<br /> Mostly he/his, sometimes she/her IRL <a href=\"https://adam-lowe.com\" target=\"_blank\">https://adam-lowe.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5291-adambeyoncelowe","name":"adambeyoncelowe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5291_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T12:46:12-07:00","id":1103883,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1103868#post1103868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As Heavy Arms explains, Hunger 0-5 is no easier to imagine than BP 0-10.</div> </div> </div> </div>He didn't explain it, he asserted it. I disagreed. Opinions vary. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>adambeyoncelowe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1017563-world-of-darkness-berlin-2017?p=1103868#post1103868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They shouldn't be purely randomised.</div> </div> </div> </div>They aren't. The rules state that the Storyteller chooses one or rolls randomly. Generally, I feel like the Storyteller is going to pick something that fits the current situation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-15T15:29:13-07:00","id":1103978,"title":"","content":"&quot;Roll or the GM picks,&quot; is to me at least, pretty backwards game design. Going back to the whole &quot;make things more 21st century gaming&quot; concept means trusting players to engage honestly with the system instead of defaulting to GM authority. Sitting back and letting the GM drive has a pretty small limit on being fun.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T02:58:48-07:00","id":1104207,"title":"","content":"If we are honest about, it literally robs the player of agency. You are told by the ST how your character feels/acts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8249-crytash","name":"Crytash","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8249_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"386"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T07:16:30-07:00","id":1104274,"title":"","content":"Player agency, as the ultimate goal of game design is overrated, IMO. I'm fine with the wording of the playtest, though I'd be also fine if it would be &quot;the player(s) and the storyteller are decifind it or if no consensus was reached, ST rolls on the table, or choose one&quot;. Sometimes, you just don't want to boggle down the game with all the negotiating between the players and ST, especially in a less intimate group and you just need the game to move forward. That's why D&amp;D 5e put so much power back in the GM's hand.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-16T14:09:52-07:00","id":1104478,"title":"","content":"Player agency isn't the &quot;ultimate goal of game design.&quot; It is an inescable aspect of player fun. Agency is a fundamental part of how humans enjoy entertainment. Obviously it plays out differently in different media, but we even see this in non-interactive entertainment (for example, a great thing to hear as feedback for non-interactive entertainment is a desire from the audience for self-insertion; that they are thinking about what they would do if they were in that or how they'd want to explore more of the universe you've created). For interactive media, agency is absolutely vital. People want to play a game when they're sold a game, not watch a movie that requires you to hit a button every few minutes. They want to have choices that matter to either gameplay and/or narrative outcomes.<br /> <br /> This doesn't mean the ultimate goal should be100% player agency, but respecting player agency is important. If you're going to take away player agency in a given section of the game, you need to make sure to provide something else to keep them invested.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}